0 corneredrat cornered_rat~

{GCornered Rat{x
{G        Bone Gnawers {W(Rank 2){x

When a Garou is backed into a corner, with nowhere to run, he can both
surrender and beg mercy, or he can fight.  This Gift allows the Garou
to focus his Rage and lash out in dire situation.  A rat- or badger-
spirit teaches this Gift.
 
{WTable Top / Role Play{x
{WSystem:{x  The character spends one Rage point and rolls her Rage
(difficulty 8).  Each success grants the character an additional die
to his Brawl pool.  When using this Gift, the werewolf automatically
enters into berserk frenzy.  This Gift lasts for the duration of
combat.
 
{WHack and Slash / Out of Character{x
{WSyntax:{c  beseech 'cornered rat'{x
While active, the Garou gains a boost to hitroll and damroll.  Also,
she gains +3 to Brawl for unarmed/claws autoattacks.  Activating this
Gift costs a point of Rage.
~
0 plaguevisage plague_visage~

{GPlague Visage{x
{G        Bone Gnawers {W(Rank 2){x
 
Anyone in his right mind fears a leper.  This Gift allows the character
to draw an illusion of terrible disease on his features, repelling even
the most stouthearted onlookers.  A useful trick for survival, it can
earn charity from a well-meaning monk, terrify locals and even serve
as a way of blending in since lepers are all but ubiquitous in some
places.  This Gift is taught by a rat-spirit.
 
{WTable Top / Role Play{x
{WSystem:{x  Roll Manipulation + Medicine (difficulty 6), the illusion
of disease lasts for one scene.  The imaginary disease may appear to
be anything that the character is familiar with, such as leprosy or
smallpox, or even something entirely invented.  Players of humans
who view the illusion must roll Willpower (difficulty 8), lest those
humans shrink away from the character in revulsion.  Supernatural
beings that are immune to disease have less to fear, so the difficulty
of their roll is only 6.
 
{WHack and Slash / Out of Character{x
{WSyntax:{c  beseech 'plague visage'{x
While this Gift's buff is active, aggressive mobs of the Garou's level
and lower will not attack her.  The Gift costs movement to activate.
~
0 cookery~

{GCookery{x
{G        Bone Gnawers {W(Rank 1){x
 
The Garou can take any small, easily destroyed item that is available
to him -- bark, moss, bones and even leather will suffice -- and stir
it into a water filled pot.  Upon activation, the stirring transmutes
the refuse into a foul-tasting, but edible, stew.  The character must
have a small pot and ladle or spoon for this Gift.  This Gift is taught
by a raccoon-spirit.
 
{WTable Top / In Character{x
{WSystem:{x  Roll Wits + Survival, difficulty depends on the ingredients
used -- 6 for inedible but otherwise harmless materials, up to 10 for
hot cinders or rusted iron.
 
{WHack and Slash / Out of Character
{WSyntax:{c  beseech 'cookery' <item>{x
{r*{c<item>{x - must be a small trash-type item.
On a difficulty 6 roll, this Gift transforms a trash item into a food
item.  The Gift costs movement to activate.
~
