0 gnaw~

{GGnaw{x
{G        Lupus {W(Rank 4){x
 
The werewolf's jaws strengthen to the point where they can chew through
nearly anything.  Her fangs inflict more damage in combat, and only death
will break her grip if she clamps down on an opponent.  Wolf-spirits teach
this Gift.
 
{WTable Top / Role Play{x
{WSystem:{x  Spend 1 Willpower point and roll Stamina +4, variable difficulty
(3 for wood, 6 for iron, 9 for steel).  The length of time required to gnaw
through something depends on the number of successes.  In addition, this
gives the character's bite two extra dice damage for the duration of the
scene.
 
{WHack and Slash / Out of Character{x
{WSyntax:{c  beseech 'gnaw'{x
While Gnaw is active, the Garou will gain +2 dice of damage on all bite attacks.
A point of Willpower must be spent to activate.
~
0 beastlife beast_life~

{GBeast Life{x
{G        Lupus / Children of Gaia {W(Rank 4){x
 
The werewolf can communicate with and even command wild animals.  Some
domesticated animals might speak to the Garou, but have given themselves
over to human masters and won't normally provide aid beyond information.
Any animal spirit can teach this Gift, although Lupus prefer to learn it
from lion- or wolf-spirits.
 
{WTable Top / Role Play{x
{WSystem:{x  Spend one Gnosis point and roll Charisma + Animal Ken,
difficulty 7.  The character gains the ability to communicate with all
animals automatically.  The animals will follow any requests the Garou
makes, although if an animal is requested to sacrifice itself, the
Garou had better pay proper homage lest she anger Gaia.  The effects
last for one scene but the player may extend the duration by spending
one Gnosis point per extra scene.
 
{WOut of Character / Hack and Slash{x
{WSyntax:{c  beseech 'beast life'{x
While the buff is active, the Garou may interact with natural animal mobs
that have 'Talk' programs on them.  Additionally, by expending movement,
she may also {yorder{x sentient natural animal mobs with a single word
command.  ({corder <mob> <command>{x)  This Gift costs 1 Gnosis to
activate.
 
{WSee also:{x  Order
~
0 laston~

{WSyntax:  {claston{x
{WSyntax:  {claston <player_name>{x
{x
The {claston{x command displays information about player logout times.
It is highly optimized to run instantaneously without server lag.
{x
{WNo Arguments:{x
Displays a summary of the most recent logouts on the server.
{x
  * {rMortals{x   - Shows the 5 most recent mortal logouts using
{x                approximate time intervals (e.g. "a short while ago").
{x                Immortal logouts are completely hidden.
{x
  * {DImmortals{x - Shows the 15 most recent player logouts (mortal and
{x                immortal) with exact, precise timestamps.
{x
{WWith a Player Name:{x
Queries the active connection or logout history of a specific player.
{x
  * {cOnline{x    - Shows exact login duration for immortals, or a
{x                generic "currently logged in" message for mortals.
{x
  * {cOffline{x   - Shows their last known logout time. If a mortal
{x                logged out within the last 5 minutes, their status is
{x                reported as "very recently logged out" for ambiguity.
{x
See Also: WHO
~
106 lootedit loottable loot_table loot_editor~

{WSyntax: {clootedit create <vnum>{x
{x        {clootedit <vnum>{x
{x
The loot-table editor (lootedit) allows builders to create randomized loot 
drops for mobiles. Each loot table has 5 slots, and each slot can be 
configured with a specific object VNUM and a drop percentage.
{x
{WCommands:{x
{cname <string>{x         : Set a descriptive name for the loot table.
{clist{x                  : List all loot tables defined in the current area.
{cshow{x                  : Display the current configuration of the loot table.
{cslot <1-5> <v> <rate>{x : Configure a loot slot.
{x
{WSlot Parameters:{x
{c<1-5>{x        : The slot number to edit (each table has 5 total).
{c<v>{x          : The VNUM of the object to drop. Use 0 to clear the slot.
{c<rate>{x       : The percentage chance (1-100) for the item to drop.
{x
{WAssigning to Mobs:{x
To make a mobile use a loot table, enter {cmedit{x for that mob and use:
{cloot <vnum>{x
Setting the loot vnum to 0 on a mob will disable randomized loot for them.
{x
{WExample Usage:{x
To create a table that has a 10% chance to drop a sword (vnum 501):
{clootedit create 500{x
{cname Low Level Soldier Loot{x
{cslot 1 501 10{x
~
106 sedit social_editor~

{WSyntax: {csedit make <name>{x
{x        {csedit <name>{x
{x
The social editor (sedit) allows you to create and modify socials at runtime.
Socials are the flavor emotes used to interact with other players (e.g., smile, 
hug, laugh). Each social consists of several different strings that are 
triggered depending on whether you have a target or are targeting yourself.
{x
{WEditable Fields (Keywords):{x
{ccnoarg{x    : {D(Char No Arg){x What YOU see when used with no target.
{conoarg{x    : {D(Others No Arg){x What OTHERS see when used with no target.
{ccfound{x    : {D(Char Found){x What YOU see when used on a target.
{cofound{x    : {D(Others Found){x What OTHERS see when used on a target.
{cvfound{x    : {D(Victim Found){x What the TARGET sees when used on them.
{ccnotfound{x : {D(Char Not Found){x What YOU see if the target isn't found.
{ccauto{x     : {D(Char Auto){x What YOU see when used on yourself.
{coauto{x     : {D(Others Auto){x What OTHERS see when used on yourself.
{x
{WSubstitution Codes:{x
{c$n{x : Your name.
{c$e{x : Your pronoun (he/she/it).
{c$m{x : Your pronoun (him/her/it).
{c$s{x : Your pronoun (his/her/its).
{c$N{x : Victim's name.
{c$E{x : Victim's pronoun (he/she/it).
{c$M{x : Victim's pronoun (him/her/it).
{c$S{x : Victim's pronoun (his/her/its).
{x
{WExample Usage:{x
To set the string for smiling at someone:
{csedit smile{x
{ccfound You smile warmly at $N.{x
{cvfound $n smiles warmly at you.{x
{cofound $n smiles warmly at $N.{x
~
0 commandtheblaze~

{GCommand the Blaze{x
{G        Warders of Men {W(Rank 5){x
Just as wood actually needs the occasional forest fire to cleanse away
the dead underbrush, cities too as raid to require the occasional blaze
to sweep away the filth and allow new life to grow.  The cities of the
Dark Medieval, however, are often tarred, thatched fire-traps.  This
Gift allows a Warder to direct the inevitable fire, urging it toward
areas that can suffer the burning and guiding it away from valuable
territory.  This Gift is taught by a fire elemental.

{WTable Top / Role Play{x
{WSystem:{x  Spend a Gnosis point, roll Willpower (diff 7).  The area
of control originates around him.  The more successes achieved, the
further the area of control stretches.

{DSuccesses  Radius of Control{x
One        Arm's reach
Two        One room
Three      A medium-sized building
Four       A city block or small keep
Five       Three city blocks; a castle
Six+       An entire city

The Warder's consciousness extends with the fire within his area of
control.  It must be one single blaze, however, rather than a number
of separate fires.  The Warder must remain still with eyes closed
and concentrate to maintain control.  If he is attacked or otherwise
distracted, the control is lost and the Gift must be initiated again
to regain control of the fire.  The fire cannot travel underwater or
across bare stone, but it can otherwise leap and twist in unnatural
fashion.  The flames can extend up to 15 feet away from their fuel
sources.

{WOut of Character / Hack and Slash{x
{WSyntax:  {cbeseech 'command the blaze' <target>{x
By spending a point of Gnosis, imbue a local fire spirit and cause
it to blast an enemy with fire.  On a critical success, the spirit
blasts the entire room.
~
0 fullmoonslight~

