{RSerpentis{x
 
This Discipline, given to the Setites by Set himself, is typically
kept within the clan and not shared to the unworthy.  They will shrug
off notions of the Discipline being a curse upon them, instead admitting
to representing the Serpent of the Garden, and are a curse upon humanity
rather than being cursed themselves.
 
This Discipline embodies the essence of temptation and corruption, by
drawing upon the powers of the Serpent of the Garden.  Many scholars
note the similarities of transformation between this power and the
Gangrel Discipline of Protean, and wonder what the founders' relationship
might have been.
 
{D    *{x Eyes of the Serpent        {chelp eyesoftheserpent{x
{D   **{x Tongue of the Asp          {chelp tongueoftheasp{x
{D  ***{x Skin of the Adder          {chelp skinoftheadder{x
{D ****{x Form of the Cobra          {chelp formofthecobra{x
{D*****{x Dark Heart                 {chelp darkheart{x
 
See also:  {WFollowersofSet{x
