{RForm of the Cobra{x
{R        Serpentis {D****{x
 
Some myths describe Set's true form as a giant cobra, hundreds of
feet long and thick as a whale.  This ability lets the Setite echo
her founder's nature by transforming into a large cobra, eight feet
long and nearly a foot thick.  The cobra is strong and swift, with
a sense of smell better than any mortal's.  Her bite carries a bite
full of poison, fatal to humans and animals (but no affect to Kindred.)
She cannot speak, but may communicate with others in this form.
 
{WTable Top / Role Play{x
{WSystem:  {xSpend a point of blood, and the transformation takes three
turns.  If three points are spent, the transformation completes in one
turn.  Attributes remain identical, but she gains two dice on rolls
involving scent, however rolls involving hearing lose two dice.  Dodge
and Climbing rolls also gain two dice to the pools.  Her bite with
natural fangs does as much damage as in human form, but carries a
seven levels of aggravated damage bonus to non-Kindred.  The change
lasts until dawn, unless desired to revert sooner.
 
{WHack and Slash / Out of Character{x
{WSyntax:  {ccobraform{x
This power costs blood to transform, and while in cobra form she gains
minor stat changes.  Additionally, she may bite in combat without having
her vampiric fangs out.  The bite also carries a chance to deal extra
poison damage on a critical strike.
~
