0 domain claim~

{WSyntax: {wClaim {c<confirm>{x
Claim by itself lets you see the influence you have in that domain. Claim
with the argument 'confirm' will try to take over the domain for your
clan. If no clan has claimed the domain, you must have 50% or higher
influence in order to claim the domain. If the domain is controlled by
another clan, you must have 30 more influence than the ruling clan to oust
them.
 
{WSyntax:{w Declare {c<relation> <clan>{x
The leader of a clan can set clan relations for that domain. The options
are "Ally", "War" or "Neutral". For example, A Tzimisce-run domain would
be set to 'war' with Tremere, while being an 'ally' of Lasombra. The
effect of this setting is that certain mobs will assist or attack members
of the clan depending on the relationship with the ruling clan. (Mobs in
a domain will already assist members of the ruling clan if they're 
influence mobs and the player is Active)
 
{WSyntax:{w tax {c<Percentage>{x
The leader of a clan can set a tax markup on all shops within the domain.
This number must be between 1 and 100. That percentage will be added to
the cost of all items in all shops within the domain, and the tax will be
deposited in the clan bank of the ruling clan.
~
