0 rage~

Garou are born with an ancient and powerful force, known as Rage,
that serves as both blessing and curse.  Rage measures the sheer
amount of primal fury seething within a Garou.  The most common
usage is to gain extra actions.  See {yprimal_urge{x for details.
Additionally, certain Gifts require Rage to activate.
 
Werewolves regain Rage in two ways on Haven of the Embraced:
{DThe Moon:{x  Upon seeing the moon in the middle of the night
{x           (must be outdoors at 12am in-game time).
{x           If your Auspice matches the current moon phase,
{x           regain your Rage to full instead of 1 point.

{D  Combat:{x  There is a small chance to regain a point when you
{x           take damage in combat.
 
{WSee also: {xPrimal_Urge Gifts Time_Ingame Auspice
~
0 gnosis~

Gnosis:
Garou, beings of both physical and spiritual, have been blessed by
Luna with a spiritual resource known as Gnosis.  Gnosis represents
a werewolf's deep ties to the spiritual world ({yumbra{x).  Many Gifts
are powered by Gnosis, and higher Gnosis makes it easier for a Garou
to enter the Umbra ({ystep_sideways{x).
 
Werewolves regain Gnosis on Haven through meditation ({ymeditation{x).
~
