This ability - available to Fera and animals - reflects instinctual
abilities that guide wild beasts.  Characters with a high rating find
it easier to tap into their wolf natures.  Garou use this to hunt,
especially while in Lupus form.  Additionally, this can be used to
induce raw, animalistic passion in others.  Primal-Urge is paired
with Stamina to {cshapeshift{x.
 
{D    *{x  Novice: Either a young animal or untrained homid Garou.
{D   **{x  Practiced: You are familiar with your animal instincts,
{D     {x             but they do not yet govern your activities.
{D  ***{x  Competent: You can slip your mind from human to beast
{D     {x             from moment to moment.
{D ****{x  Expert: Your wolf nature guides you without your
{D     {x          consciously choosing to do so.
{D*****{x  Master: You are closely tied to Gaia and the Wyld.
 
Possessed by:  Werewolves, Wild Animals, Hunters
Specialties:  Shifting Forms, Hunting, Animal Attraction
 
{R*{WOut of Character / Hack and Slash{x
{WSyntax:  {crage{x
By spending a point of Rage, a Garou taps into her primal instincts
to increase her speed and ferocity.  She gains a number of extra
attacks per combat round equal to her Primal-Urge rating.
 
See also:  Rage Shapeshift
~
