In order to activate a Gift that a Garou has learned, she must beseech
the spirits of that Gift and request permission to use the intended effect.
In Character, each Gift is taught by a specific type of Spirit, and this
is usually the same Spirit that a Garou is requesting to.  
 
The standard format for beseeching is as follows:
{WSyntax:  {cbeseech 'giftnamehere' <option>{x
 
{R*{x See help files for individual gifts for specific details.

See Also:  {WGifts Garou{x
~
0 camouflage_discernment camouflagediscernment~

{CCamouflage Discernment{x
{C        Correspondence {D*{x, {CLife {D*{x, {CMind {D*{x
 
A Mage must face many perils daily and nightly, both from threats seen
and unseen.  With a combination of Correspondence, Life, and Mind, some
Mages have learned how to determine where an enemy may be hiding nearby.
By detecting thoughts nearby, she can pinpoint locations and read the
errant Life Patterns around her.
 
{WTable Top / Role Play{x
{WSystem:  {xWith a successful Effect, the Mage can pinpoint where a hidden
enemy is.  She can add her successes to her Perception roll (if needed) when
trying to determine the exact location of a hiding entity.
 
{WOut of Character / Hack and Slash{x
{WSyntax:  {crote 'camouflage discernment'{x
With a successful Arete roll, this rote grants the ability to detect hidden
mobs and players, whether hiding from normal or supernatural means.  You
must be reasonably close to your target's level, or higher level.
 
See Also: {WMage Mind Sphere{x
~
0 matter_perception matterperception~

