0 rote_betterbody betterbody better_body~

{CBetter Body{x
{C       Life {W***{x
 
Practicioners of Life to this degree understand their own Pattern well
enough to begin affecting changes to their own body.  Small changes
can be made, such as giving themselves gills or making cosmetic alterations.
Additionally, small changes to physical traits can be made to increase
the mage's prowess.
 
{WTable Top / Role Play{x
{WSyntax:{x The Mage rolls her Arete, and the successes earned determines
the extent of the alterations and the duration.  Minor cosmetic alterations
or creating gills is a simple effect, whereas swapping two physical traits
may take a bit more effort.
 
{WOut of Character / Hack and Slash{x
{WSyntax: {crote 'better body'{x
Only needing a simple Arete roll, the Mage alters her physical traits.  On
a successful roll, she increases her Strength, Dexterity, and Stamina all
by one for a duration.
~
0 refinematter refine_matter rote_refinematter~

{CRefine Matter{x
{C        Matter {W*****{x
 
{WSyntax: {crote 'refine matter' <object>{x
{R          Note{W* {yobject: weapon, helm, chest, leggings{x
 
A Master of Matter has learned how to manipulate an object's Pattern
to the point of defying all laws of physics.  By imbuing an item with
Quintessence via Prime, she can create powerful equipment beyond normal
means of reality.  By manipulating how an object interacts with the
Patterns surrounding her, a Mage can alter the properties of physical
items.  The most common uses of this are increasing the deadliness of
a weapon, or reinforcing the defensive capabilities of armor.
 
{WTable Top / Role Play:{x
{WSyntax: {xThe Mage rolls Arete (difficulty varies), and the amount of
successes determines how much the item can be changed.  Major transformations
tend to be quite vulgar and usually reserved for occasions when the Mage
needs permanent special objects.
 
{WOut of Character / Hack and Slash:{x
{WSyntax: {xWith a successful roll, the Mage can empower either a weapon, or
certain pieces of armor, with additional power.  Empowering a weapon gives
more damage, while pieces of armor give more defense.  The empowerment lasts
for some time, and you cannot enhance an already imbued item.  Four types of
equipment are able to be enhances: weapon, helmet, chest, leggings.
 
See also:  Sphere_Matter
~
