{D    *  {c 'of the opened caern'{x - Gain the blessing of the Caern.
{x                                *Requires a heart.
{D ****  {c'of the opened bridge'{x - Enter the Moon Bridge path to travel to
{x                                other Caerns in the world.
{x                                *Requires a warpstone.
~
109 globalpower~

Do not use the doubleexp command by itself without adding global XP.
It will check, 0 or negative values will reset the value to 0 and disable double XP.
If you want to manually provide extra XP, add XP manually and activate it,
or let it autoproc.  Or if it's greater than 300k it will auto enable on
first kill)
~
0 hometown~

Haven has a number of recall points that you can set as your hometown. 
Your default hometown is Chester, where you will recall to Sir Owen. 
However, if you wish to set other locations, you can periodically change
your hometown using Quest Points.  The command to access the hometown menu
gives listing and details to see which cities are available.  
 
{WSyntax: {yhometown{x
 
{WSee Also:  Recall{x
~
0 perceive_entropy perceiveentropy~

{CPerceive Entropy{x
{C       Entropy {W*{x
 
{WSyntax:  {crote 'perceive entropy' <target>{x
 
Rudimentary knowledge of Entropic energies allows a mage to view the
current of destiny flowing in the universe in relation to objects and
beings.  She can sense the impact of fate, where chance is altered or
nudged.  Additionally, by sensing the flow of Entropy, she can determine
weak points in her target.
 
{WTable Top / Role Play{x
{WSystem:  {xSuccesses on an Arete roll allows a Mage to locate areas of
chaos, disorder, and decay.  By focusing on a Pattern, she may determine
a target's weakest point, or sensing the alteration of chance and Fate.
The higher number of successes achieved, the more detail is gleaned.
 
{WOut of Character / Hack and Slash{x
{WSystem:  {xBy sensing the Entropic energies around your foe, you can
determine possible mystical alterations favoring/hindering an opponent's
Fate.  Additionally, with further successes, a Mage can detect a target's
weaknesses, and possibly even determine how far along her opponent is
to death and demise.
 
See also:  {WEntropy{x
~
0 pack_tactics packtactics~

{GPack Tactics{x
{W       (Requires two or more Garou in a group.){x

Garou are pack animals, and many of their strengths come from working in
numbers.  Moving as a cohesive group, many Garou have developed tactics to
take advantage of their close knit society.  Different tactics allow for
different outcomes.
 
{WSyntax:  {cpacktactics <target> <tactic>{x
{R*{DCurrent Tactics: {Wsavage{x
{R*{DAll tactics require the initiating Garou to spend 1 Willpower.{x
 
{rSavage{x:  The initiating Garou knocks the target down.  On successful knockdown,
the other Garou in the group get a free bite attack on the target.  While the
initial werewolf can be in any form, the ones who wish to join must be in Crinos,
Hispo, or Lupus form to be able to effectively bite the target.
~
