{C       Time {W*{x
 
The first initiation of a Mage into understanding Time, as might be expected,
is an awareness of time's flow.  The mage learns to discern subjective time,
keep accurate track of time, as well as notice abnormalities and alterations
through the disturbances left in the temporal 'wake' of such effects.

{WTable Top / Role Play{x
{WSystem:{x  With a bit of concentration, a Mage can detect the minor ripples
left behind in the flow of time from mystical effects.  Keeping up senses
to detect these ripples constantly can be trying, but if a Mage suspects that
time alteration has taken place, with extended concentration they can discern
the main details of the underlying currents.
 
{WHack and Slash / Out of Character{x
{WSyntax:  {crote 'time sense'{x
By attuning oneself to the ebb and flow of Time, the Mage senses when
Time has been altered.  This rote allows a Mage to see when someone has been
{D({YAccelerated{D){x {Y({DDecelerated{Y) {xor {Y[{DStopped{Y]{x through supernatural means.
~
