0 drain~

{yDrain{x
{W       [Requires an empty vial]{x

Ghouls must feed upon Kindred Vitae to continue their existence as
servants of their masters.  While this is usually given willingly by
the Domitor, occasionally one finds themselves without a supply at hand.
The easiest way to ensure you have a stock of vampire blood ready is to
drain the vitae from a torpored vampire into an empty vial for later use.
 
A successful drain will provide a vial of kindred blood{R*{x for consumption,
while a botch will outright kill your target, wasting the blood.  Knowledge
of Medicine is not required to do this, but knowledge of where to pierce
the best arteries and veins increases your chances.
 
Anyone can use this ability, but Vampires and especially Ghouls benefit the
most from draining and collecting Vitae.
 
{WSyntax:  {cdrain <target>{x
 
{R*{xThe vials of vitae collected are considered 'potions'.

See Also:  {WVampire Ghoul Blood Vitae Torpor Behead{x
