0 shed~

{GShed{x
{G        Metis {W(Rank 1){x
 
The metis can shed a layer of fur and skin, slipping from an opponent's
grasp or escaping from bonds with ease.  A lizard-spirit or snake-
spirit teaches this Gift.
 
{WTable Top / Role Play{x
{WSystem:{x  The player rolls Dexterity + Primal-Urge (diff 7).  If the roll
succeeds, the character loses a tuft of fur, allowing her to slip free of
grapples or bonds such as ropes or chains (-2 difficulty on any such
rolls).
 
{WHack and Slash / Out of Character{x
{WSyntax:  {cbeseech 'shed'{x
The player must spend a single point of Willpower and roll Dexterity +
Primal-Urge, difficulty 7.  On success, for the duration, the garou is
resistant to blunt/bashing attacks as the attacks tend to slip off of
the loose fur, lowering the effectiveness of the attack.
