0 classify~

{yClassify{x
{y       Animal Ken {W*{x
 
The supernatural are not the only denizens in the world.  Many creatures
found in nature roam the countryside, or hide in the dark corners of the
cities.  With a bit of careful study, one can learn much about the natural
order of the animal kingdom.  This ability allows the player to to recall
information from studies, and personal experiences, about natural animals
in the world.
 
{WTable Top / Role Play{x
{WSystem:{x  The player rolls Intelligence + Animal Ken (difficulty 7) to
determine the information that she has learned over the course of her
studies, whether through having official studying of books or firsthand
experiences.  The amount of successes determines the amount of detail
recalled.  One success allows identification of race, whereas additional
successes can provide habits, offensive capabilities, and other bits
of information.
 
{WOut of Character / Hack and Slash{x
{WSystem:  {xSame as prior.  More successes will provide more information.
Only usable on natural members of the animal kingdom, not including
humanoids.  The ability costs movement to carefully study your target.
 
{WSyntax:  {cclassify <target>{x
