102 attr_flag attribute_flag attrflag attributeflag~

Mobs on Haven have access to a limited character sheet for determining
dicepools, just as players do.  The MUD is hardcoded to create a mob's
character sheet at the moment a mob loads, based upon a number of random
factors.  In addition to the randomly generated character sheet, we can
set additional bonuses to mob Attributes that get added after the mob
is loaded.
 
Strong          +3 STR, +2 DEX, +2 STA
Weak            -3 STR, -2 DEX, -2 STA
Social          +3 CHA, +2 MAN, +2 APP
Awkward         -3 CHA, -2 MAN, -2 APP
Brilliant       +2 PER, +3 INT, +2 WIT
Dull            -2 PER, -3 INT, -2 WIT
Allplustwo      +2 ALL ATTRIBUTES
Allminustwo     -2 ALL ATTRIBUTES
Allplusfour     +4 ALL ATTRIBUTES
Allminusfour    -4 ALL ATTRIBUTES
Crinos          +4 STR, +1 DEX, +3 STA, MAN = 0, APP = 0
~
0 callofthewyld call_of_the_wyld~

{GCall of the Wyld{x
{G       Galliard {W(Rank 1){x
 
This gift augments a Garou's communication through howls.  A Garou can
howl a cry that stirs and invigorates other werewolves, even far beyond
the normal range of hearing.  This Gift is commonly used to open a revel,
or to call for aid in times of peril.  A wolf-spirit teaches this Gift.
 
{WTable Top / Role Play{x
{WSystem:  {xThe player rolls Stamina + Empathy, the number of successes
determines how far away the Call can be heard and how stirring it is.
This can be used in concert with any standard Garou howls.  The Story-
teller determines the actual effects, but they should be linked to the
type of howl made and the intent of the Garou.  Some examples are: Wyrm
agents are distracted by the howl, all Garou in the area do not hesitate
to respond to the Call for Succor, or those at the revel earn extra die
to their dice pools during the revel.
 
{WHack and Slash / Out of Character{x
{WSyntax:  {cbeseech 'call of the wyld'{x
All Garou in your group hear the call and join in the call to Luna.
Each participant gains a bonus to Strength, and a critical on
the roll gives Stamina as well.  This Gift requires movement to use.
~
0 breathofthewyld breath_of_the_wyld~

{GBreath of the Wyld{x
{G       Black Furies {W(Rank 1){x
 
Black Furies believe the problem with most humans (and some Garou)
is that they have forgotten that the energy of Creation is nourishing
in addition to destructive.  With this Gift, a Black Fury can impart
a feeling of life and vitality into a living being.  A spirit servant
of Pegasus teaches this Gift.
 
{WTable Top / Role Play{x
{WSystem:  {xThe Fury must touch her target's skin, and this Gift must
be used outdoors in a natural setting (a park is natural enough for
this).  The player rolls Gnosis (difficulty 6 for humans, 5 for Garou).
Success grants a rush of energy and clarity of thought.  This grants
one extra die on all Mental rolls for the next scene.  It also adds
one to the difficulty of any Rage rolls the target makes in that time.
 
{WHack and Slash / Out of Character{x
{WSystem:  {xThis Gift can only target living beings.  On successful roll,
target gains +1 to all Mental CS Stats.  The room you are in must be
a natural setting for the Gift to work.  This can be used on yourself
in addition to others.
 
{WSyntax:  {cbeseech 'breath of the wyld' <target>{x
~
102 obj_extra_chart objextrachart object_extra_chart objectextrachart~

Objects in the MUD can be set with a variety of flags to interact with
the rest of the environment.  Some affect visibility, others affect
combat, and still others just add flavor.
 
glow - You can see the item on the ground or in your inventory, without
the need of an external light.
hum - Does nothing.  [DO NOT USE]
dark - Does nothing.  [DO NOT USE]
hidden - Flag used to keep ore veins for mining hidden until discovered.  [DO NOT USE]
illuminate - item can be seen same as glowing, additionally when in room
adds to light in room for seeing.
invis - item can only be seen with detect_invis [DO NOT USE]
magic - Flag for extra enhanced magical items, shows up for detect_magic spell [DO NOT USE]
nodrop - Item is cursed and cannot be dropped, until de-cursed
bless - Item is holy, cannot be used by vampires
pausetimer - Flag that prevents timer from deducting when obj is not equipped
reflective - Mirrored surface, chance of casting reflection when entering room/looking at object.
{Rscaling{x - UNCODED.
noremove - Cannot be removed from a character.  [DO NOT USE]
inventory - Items flagged inventory cannot be stolen, and are immediately removed upon a mob's death.
nopurge - Prevents item from being able to be immortal-purged. [DO NOT USE]
rotdeath - Item gets set a timer upon character death, and will crumble
visdeath - Item is undetectable until mob is killed and looking in corpse.
rare - Item has 50% chance of load on reset [Discuss first]
nonmetal - flags item having no metal, prevents being affected by 'heat metal' spell
meltdrop - Object immediately destroys itself upon being dropped.
hadtimer - Flag used by the code for objects with timers to crumble.  [DO NOT USE]
sellextract - Item is destroyed when bought by a merchant, instead of going to merchant's inventory.
burnproof - Obj not destroyed by fire/ice/acid/shock attacks, cannot be poisoned, immune to heat metal spell.
nouncurse - cannot be uncursed [DO NOT USE]
isstake - item is a stake [currently unused as staking was removed]
ispreserve - Allows players to dip items into this object to preserve deteriorating items. [Discuss first]
isenhanced - Certain powers/skills alter an object, this flags an object as altered to keep from double-altering.  [DO NOT USE]
brew - Flags a potion as a brewed item. [DO NOT USE]
umbra - Flags an item as Umbral.  Do not load umbral items onto non-umbral mobs, or vice versa.  [RESTRICTED - discuss first and have a good reason for it to be umbral if not an umbral area]
~
0 merge_localities mergelocalities~

{CMerge Localities{x
{C       Correspondence {W*****{x
 
{WSyntax:  {crote 'merge localities' <target>{x
 
{WTable Top / Role Play{x
{WSystem:  {xAt this level of understanding, the Mage can cause two individual
objects, entities, or even entire locations to overlap each other and exist
in the same space simultaneously.  Both instances can be interacted with as
normal, and are completely real and solid to each other.  However, they do
not cause damage to each other while occupying the same space.  Refer to the
Correspondence Chart ({ycorr_chart{x) to determine difficulties.
 
{WOut of Character / Hack and Slash{x
{WSystem:  {xOn a successful Arete roll, difficulty determined by target's room,
the mage creates two gates.  One in the originating room, and one in the
target's room.  Each gate leads to the other location, and the duration is a
bit longer than the gate created by Correspondence 4 (Conjoin Localities).
 
{WSee also:  Corr_Chart Conjoin_Localities Sphere_Correspondence{x
~
0 corr_chart corrchart~

Determining a Correspondence effect's success is largely based upon
the Mage's familiarity with the target of the effect.  Range would be
used for geographical/spacial locations as the target, whereas if the
target is a person or object, the Mage's connection to the target is
then used.

{BSuccesses{y==={BRange{y================{BConnection{y==========================={x
One         Line of sight        Body Sample
Two         Very familiar        Close possession or companion
Three       Familiar             Possession or casual friend
Four        Visited once         Acquaintance or object used once
Five        Described location   Briefly touched or met object/person
Six+        Anywhere on Earth    No connection
{y======================================================================{x
 
{WSee also:  CORRESPONDENCE SPHERE{x
~
0 sevenleaguestride seven_league_stride~

{CThe Seven League Stride{x
{x       {CCorrespondence {W***{x
 
{WSyntax:  {crote 'seven league stride' <target>{x
 
{WTable Top / Role Play{x
{WSystem:  {xThe mage bends the laws of physical space, bending and folding
reality in upon itself, briefly causing two physical points in space to
connect, and thereby steps from one location to another.  See the help
file for the Correspondence Chart ({ycorr_chart{x) for the total number of
successes required for the effect to take place.
 
{WHack and Slash / Out of Character{x
{WSystem:  {xThe mage must make a successful Arete roll, difficulty is
based upon the target's room.  If a target is in a safe room, as an
example, then the transition will fail automatically.  You must be able
to see your target to attempt a Seven League Stride.
~
0 vitae~

A vampire must feed upon the blood of the living in order to survive.
Once ingested, a Kindred's body transmutes the blood into a more potent
form, known as vitae.  Vitae takes on a mystical quality, becoming much
more than just normal blood.  Vitae sustains a vampire's body, for with-
out it, she would wither away.
 
Vitae is used to fuel multiple supernatural powers available to vampires.
From Regeneration, to mystical Disciplines, the phrase "Blood is Life"
holds especially true.  Feeding upon the blood of the living or recently
deceased is the most common means of replenishing your supply.
 
Review the help file for {Rvampire{x for additional information.
 
See also:  {WVampire Bloodpool Feed{x
~
0 tasteofdeath taste_of_death spitblood spit_blood~

{RTaste of Death{x
{R       Quietus {W*****{x
 
A refinement of Baal's Caress, Taste of Death allows the Cainite to
spit caustic blood at her target. The blood coughed forth with this
power burns flesh and corrodes bone; some vampires have been
reported to vomit voluminous streams of vitae that reduce their
targets to heaps of sludge.
 
{WTable Top / Role Play{x
{WSystem:{x  The vampire may spit up to 10 feet for each dot of Strength
and Potence he possesses.  Hitting the target requires a Stamina +
Athletics roll (Diff: 6).  Each point of vitae spent (up to per-turn
max) inflicts 2 dice of aggravated damage.
 
{WHack and Slash / Out of Character{x
{WSyntax:  {cspitblood <target>{x
This attack does acid damage, and requires blood to activate.  The
lower your Generation, the more blood must be spent, however this
also increases the damage roll.
 
See also: Assamite Quietus
~
0 gauntlet_chart gauntletchart~

{GGauntlet {CChart{x:
 
The Gauntlet's thickness varies from place to place, depending on the
level of spiritual energy permeating a location.  Below is a general
chart to give a quick look at the relative difficulty rating of typical
areas.  Additionally, the minimum number of successes required to
pierce the Gauntlet at such a location is also provided.

{R*{GGarou{x When 'Stepping Sideways', you must make a Gnosis roll against
the room's Gauntlet Rating.
{R*{CMages {xWhen using Spirit Sphere rotes, you must gain a number of
successes on a standard Arete roll.

{D<-------------------------------------------------------------------->{x
{W   Area        Type          Rating       Successes{x
~
0 control_gauntlet controlgauntlet~

{CControl Gauntlet{x
{C       Spirit {W****{x
 
{WSyntax:  {crote 'control gauntlet'{x

At this level of mastery of the Sphere of Spirit, a mage can alter the
very spiritual membrane which separates the physical world from that
of the Umbral.  With enough practice and magic fueling the rote, a mage
can tear open a temporary rift between layers, providing passage across
the Gauntlet.  While the rift is open, any sentient beings may make use
of it.
 
{WTable Top / Role Play{x
{WSystem:  {xThe mage must garner successes based upon the Gauntlet rating.
 
{WHack and Slash / Out of Character{x
{WSystem:  {xThe mage must acquire a number of successes based upon the
Gauntlet rating of the room.  If successful, temporary rifts will allow
passage to the Umbra, and back from the Umbra, at the location.
~
0 glower rbf~

{yGlower{x
{y      Intimidation {W***{x
 
{WSyntax:  {cglower{x

Brute strength and harsh words are often quite effective at dissuading
others from bothering oneself.  However, a well performed constant glower
presents the face of someone who is not to be messed with.  Just the simple
look upon your face conveys enough of your mood to prevent all but the most
foolish from bothering you.
 
{WTable Top / Role Play{x
{WSystem:  {xTypically a Courage roll would be called for by the target with
being able to resist someone trying to intimidate.  The player rolls
Charisma + Intimidate, and anyone who tries to oppose her during the scene
would need to score more successes on a Courage roll than the player garnered.
 
{WOut of Character / Hack and Slash{x
{WSystem:  {xThis ability costs 1 Willpower to activate.  With a Charisma +
Intimidation roll (difficulty varies), you project a look to everyone nearby
which conveys a bit of fear and determination.  Mobs up to your level will
leave you alone for the duration.
~
0 gauntlet~

{GThe Gauntlet{x:
Between the individual layers of the Umbra, as well as separating the
Umbra from the physical world, is a thin spiritual membrane that prevents
most entities from crossing between layers.  This membrane is called the
Gauntlet, and varies from location to location.  Areas of high spiritual
energy, sites of intense emotions, or areas filled with ambient magic tend
to have a much thinner membrane than areas of mundanity and order.  The
thinner the membrane, the lower the rating of the Gauntlet, and the easier
it is to cross over between the Physical Realm and the Umbral Realm.
 
{GGauntlet Rating:{x
The Guantlet is rated on a scale from 3 to 10, with 3 being places of intense
power and 10 being areas such as the middle of a fortress in a large city.
Most beings that can traverse across the Gauntlet will need to accumulate a
number of successes based upon the Gauntlet Rating at the location.  The
number of successes needed can be found on the {ygauntlet_chart{x.
 
See also: {WUmbra Gauntlet_Chart{x
~
0 umbra~

{GThe Umbra:{x
The physical world upon which we live is only one of many planes that co-
exist at once, all layered across each other and comprising reality.  The
additional layers of existence lie just beyond most mortals' reach, and
even out of reach of most supernatural beings.  Comprising of the realm of
the dead, the realm of the Abyss, the spiritual reflection of the physical
world...  All of these layers and more are collectively called the Umbra.

{YState of the Umbra on Haven:{x
Forces throughout the world have been set in motion, causing the planes
of the Umbra to begin merging together.  While once layered and seperated by
the thin protection between each realm called the Gauntlet, the individual
realms of existence have begun fusing together with their neighboring areas.
The result is a twisted mashup of spiritual and magical layers overlapping
each other, ultimately colliding into a single layer of pure chaos.  The
Umbra, in all of its various forms, was never a safe place to traverse under
the best of conditions for the average traveller.  With this overlay, many
new entities have begun springing forth and populating the various locations
that were previously undisturbed.  The Shadowlands have begun overlaying
portions of Arcadia, the Penumbra merging with every other layer in the
vicinity, and so forth.  The combinations are as numberous as the layers
themselves.  No two locations are meshed exactly the same.  During all of
this turmoil, many inhabitants of the Umbral layers whom were previously
stranded in the physical layer of reality, have been inextricably pulled
back to their native Umbralscape by the sheer force of the merging.  Some
have gone willingly and welcomed the chance to cross over to their home
realm, while others rail against this development even now, striving to find
ways to cross back to the material plane.  Whatever the cause, this
coalescing of realms into a single Umbral layer likely spells trouble for
the denizens of the plane, and it is only a matter of time before the
dangers of this new Umbral realm flow into the material plane once again.  
 
{BAccessing the Umbra:{x
{GGarou:       {xStepping Sideways
{RVampires:    {xAuspex 5 (Astral Projection)
{CMages:       {xSpirit 3 (Step Sideways), Spirit 4 (Control Gauntlet)
All Others:  Ask a Mage with Spirit 4, Various Umbral rifts
~
0 destroymatter destroy_matter~

{CDestroy Matter{x
{C       Entropy {W***{x
 
{WSyntax:  {crote 'destroy matter' {w<target>{x
 
At this level of Entropy, the mage can accelerate the decay of items to
proportions unseen in nature.  Projecting an entropic field around a small
object, the ravages of natural decay take over and destroy the object in
record time.
 
{WTable Top / Role Play{x
{WSystem:{x  The number of successes scored on the Mage's Arete roll would
determine the size of the object able to be affected and the speed at which
it would decay.

{x  Successes    Rate of Decay
{x      1          One Week
{x      2          One Day
{x      3          One Hour
{x      4          One Minute
{x      5+         One Second
 
{WOut of Character / Hack and Slash{x
{WSystem:  {xUsing this rote, a Mage can destroy an opponent's weapon, shield,
or held item.  Upon activation, the effect automatically targets in this order:
weapon, shield, held.  If an object is not found on your target, it automatically
attempts to target the next item.  If none of the three are equipped by your
target, the rote does nothing.
 
See also:  {WEntropy Rote{x
~
