102 flagfind~

Syntax is : flagfind <obj/mob/room> <type> <flag>
Obj types : extra, wear, affect, damage, type, weapon, special, spell,
{x            size, level, cost
Mob types : level, race, special, shop, aff, aff2, act, act2, off, res, 
{x            vuln, imm, attr, abil
Room types: sector, room, clan, owner
{x
Flagfind is a useful utility to find all mobs/objects/rooms in the MUD matching
a specific flag or type. It outputs a list of matching results after searching 
every vnum. The results show four columns.
{x
{cSpecial Syntax:{x
'{Dflagfind mob level{x' has the following special syntax:
{R*{x mob level 10 - Find all mobs whose level = level 10.
{R*{x mob level above 10 - level is OVER 10.
{R*{x mob level below 10 - level is up to, not including 10.
{R*{x mob level between 1 10 - Level is above 1, less than 10, exclusive.
{R**{x This means that 'between 1 10' will display mobs levels 2, 3, 4, 5,
{x   6, 7, 8, 9. But NOT 1 or 10. If you wished to see all mobs whose levels
{x   were 1-10 including 1 and 10, you'd have to use 'level between 0 11'.
{R*** {WThis is also syntax for 'obj level' and 'obj cost'{x
{x
'{Dflagfind mob special{x' has the following special syntax:
{R*{x mob special spec_fido - You must include 'spec_' on the function.
 
'flagfind room owner' has the following special option:
{R* {Wroom owner all {x- Will list all rooms with an owner.
~
