0 globalxp gxp doublexp dxp triplexp txp~

{D         [{WGlobal Experience Pool{D]{x
Haven of the Embraced has a system in place to automatically trigger
mudwide bonus sessions of Double Experience or even Triple Experience.
The current pool of global experience on the MUD can be found on the
'who' list, under MUD stats.

When a mob is killed, 10% of the XP a player gains from the kill is
added to the global XP pool.  This 10% addition also triggers during
RP, based on the amount of XP you earned during your time in IC Mode.
If the Global XP then meets or exceeds specific thresholds after the
addition, the MUD will automatically check to determine if the session
is triggered for that threshold.  If yes, an announcement will display
and the pool will begin to drain.  If no, the MUD will check at the next
threshold.

{y[{W Threshold - Chance - Multiplier{y ]{x
{x   150k XP  -   25%  -     2X
{x   200k XP  -   40%  -     2X
{x   225k XP  -   55%  -     2X
{x   250k XP  -   70%  -     2X
{x   275k XP  -   85%  -     2X
{x   300k XP  -  100%  -     3X

During a Double/Triple session, the 'bonus' XP that you earn on top of
the base XP awarded gets deducted out of the global pool.  For example,
during 2X a mob that awards 100xp will instead award 200xp, and 100xp is
deducted.   During 3X, you would earn 300xp and 200xp is deducted.  This
amount is deducted on a per player basis based on the XP that the player
earned.  When the global pool reaches 0xp, the session automatically ends
and experience earned will begin filling the pool once again.

{WSee also:  Experience{x
~
0 directions dirs~

To aid in getting around, the following speedwalking directions have been
submitted and published for anyone to use.  They may not be the most direct
way to get somewhere, and there is always the possibility of getting
waylayed or attacked by MOBs on the paths.  But the following directions
will give a basic idea of where players can go to gain experience in each of
the geographic areas.  
 
Chester Directions:     help {cchester_dirs{x
Geneva Directions:      help {cgeneva_dirs{x
Copenhagen Directions:  help {ccopenhagen_dirs{x
Venice Directions:      help {cvenice_dirs{x
~
0 letter letters~

Haven sports a letter writing system.
Requirements:
Reading letters - Academics @0000
Writing letters - Academics @@000
Sealing letters - Resources @0000 or Status @0000
 
You can purchase a blank letter from Owen at Chester's recall.
Hold the paper in your hand, and use the command 'write' to write to it.
E.G write This is cool
 
Be warned, it's a single shot item, like writing on paper is. You get one line (At a reasonable length and can use the return character)
 
To seal it, type 'seal' This way if it is to be delivered to a specific person, they will know if it's been opened.
If it's sealed and unopened, you can verify the sender.
(People can't fake seals..for now)
~
0 shout~

Shout is a global channel heard by anyone on the MUD.  Most players
prefer the use of the OOC channel.  
~
0 arise~

{rArise{x
{W        (Vampire in Torpor){x

Arise is an innate vampiric ability to force oneself out of {ytorpor{x
without the aid of another.  Players with a --{WNewbie{x-- flag have an
increased chance of success on the use of this command.  Use of
this ability is unlimited, but you will not be able to attempt
to {carise{x until your torpor affect has worn off (seen on your
{yaffects{x screen).
 
{WSyntax:  {carise{x
 
See also:  Torpor Affects
~
0 weapon_skills~

The weapon skills on Haven are divided into four general categories.
Each weapon skill starts with a base of 50%, current and maximum.
Each dot invested in the broader category increases the maximum level
attainable by each skill by ten percent, with 5 dots invested yielding
a maximum of 100% proficiency possible.  Your current proficiency
raises through usage, up to your current attainable maximum in the
category.  The higher your proficiency, the higher success rate of
your autoattacks with that type of weapon.
 
They are as follows:
- Light
-- Dagger and Whip
 
- Heavy
-- Axe and Sword
 
- Blunt
-- Flail and Mace
 

- Polearm
-- Lance, Polearm, and Spear
 
{R*{xThere exists a weapon type that does not follow the normal rate
of proficiencies.  The 'exotic' weapon type can be used by anyone,
regardless of proficiency.  Your weapon proficiency when using an
exotic weapon is always considered equal to base 50%, plus 5% for
each point in Melee that you possess.  This proficiency does not
increase via usage, it may only be raised by purchasing more dots
in your Melee skill.  You tradeoff maximum potential for not having
to specialize in something specific.

- Exotic
-- Varies
~
0 skill_map skills_map skills_table skill_table dot_map~

This helpfile has been replaced by the skillmap command.  To see a list
of skills and their cs dot requirements, use the syntax below.  This command
reads from the CS Skill Table in the code, so it will auto-update any time a
skill is added.  
 
