0 sensespirit sense_spirit spiritsight spirit_sight sense spirit sight~

{CSpirit Sight{x
{C       Spirit {W*{x

Attuning oneself to the Spiritual Realms, a Mage can shift his senses
to view across the spiritual barrier between the layers of existence.
Piercing through the Gauntlet and seeing into the other side, only
allows you to view the Umbral plane.  It does not allow the Mage to
interact with the Umbra in any way.  Higher knowledge of Spirit is
required to actually affect the Umbra.
 
{WTable Top / Role Play{x
{WSystem:{x  The amount of successes acquired on an Arete roll determines
the number of senses that the Mage can project across to the Umbral
plane.
 
{WOut of Character / Hack and Slash{x
{WSyntax:  {crote 'spirit sight'{x
Spirit Sight allows the Mage to detect any entities or objects
existing just across the Gauntlet and in the Umbral layer of the MUD.
Additionally, she can detect the relative thickness of the Umbra in
a given location [Gauntlet Rating].
 
See also:  {WSpirit Umbra Gauntlet{x
~
0 rote_timealteration time_alteration timealteration~

{CTime Alteration{x
{C       Time {W***{x

With this level of mastery, a Mage can alter the apparent flow of time at
a localized site.  By dilating or contracting time, she can alter the rate
that things happen in relation to "The Real World".  The subject is not
changed, only the subjective time surrounding the target.

{WIn Character / Role Play{x
{WSystem: {xFor every success on the Mage's Arete roll, she can perform a
physical action on the following turn.  The extra actions take place
at the end of Combat, after all other actions are done.  Each action uses
a full dice pool, no splitting required.

{WOut of Character / Hack and Slash{x
{WSyntax: {crote 'time alteration'{x
This rote alters the Patterns of Time around a Mage's own body, just
enough to allow the Mage to speed up and take additional attacks.  The
greater the Mage's understanding of Time, the more potential attacks are
possible while this rote is active.
~
0 rote_precognition precognition~

{CPrecognition{x
{C        Time {W**{x

The usage of this rote will allow the Initiate of Time to sense what
is about to happen, just prior to it happening.  The usual manifestation
of this is the ability to sidestep incoming attacks, such as kicks.
The Mage gets a brief flash of insight as a warning of what is to
come, and may react accordingly.
 
{WTable Top / Role Play{x
{WSystem: {xWith a simple Time Effect, the Mage gains glimpses of what
is to come, moments before it actually happens.  The Storyteller
describes the most likely scenario incoming, and the Mage can then
use that brief moment of knowledge to her advantage.  The more
successes scored, the further in advance the flash of insight is.
 
{WHack and Slash / Out of Character{x
{WSyntax: {crote 'precognition'{x
While the rote is active, reduce the attack rolls of incoming kicks,
bashes, dirt kicks, trips, bites, disarms.  It also reduces the
rolls on some 'special programs' on certain mobs.
~
