0 lagged dazed stunned~

Certain actions can place a target and / or player into a lagged state
known as lag.  To a certain part, all skills and spells have differing
amounts of lag involved with them.
{x
Some skills and spells however are capable of not only inducing lag, but
even stop automatic hits during combat as well.  While stopped or stunned
the player, or mobile will stand there completely doing nothing; they will
be unable to execute an action.  Once the duration of stun has expired
they, the player or mobile, will be able to execute an action again. 
~
0 auraperception aura_perception~

{RAura Perception{x {W|{x {RAura Sight{x
     {RAuspex{x {W**{x
              
This power reveals psychic auras, that radiate from mortals and supernatural
beings alike.  These halos comprise a shifting series of colors that take
practice to discern with clarity.  Even the simplest individual has many 
shiftinghues within his aura, but current emotions predominate.  Momentary 
impressions or deep secrets flash through in streaks and swirls.  The colors
change in sympathy with the subject's emotional state, blending into new tones
in a constantly dancing pattern.  The stronger the emotions involved, the more
intense the hues become.  A skilled vampire can learn much from her subject by
reading the nuances of color and brilliance in the aura's flow.
           
Aside from perceiving emotional states, vampires use Aura Perception to detect 
supernatural beings.  The colors in Kindred auras, while intense, are usually
quite pale.  Awakaned mages aura's flare and crackle with suppressed power.
Garou and the other Changing Breeds have strikingly bright, almost frantic, 
halos.  If a Wraith can be read with this power it's aura is weak and flickers
like a dying flame, while Faerie creatures radiate halos in rainbow hues.
         
{WTable Top / Role Play{x
{WSystem:{x Perception + Empathy {WDiff:{x {R8{x-{R10{x
Each success indicates how much of the aura the character sees and can
understand.   Failure reveals nothing, and a botch gives the vampire totally
false and misleading information.  It is possible, although more difficult,
to sense the aura of a being who is otherwise invisible to normal sight, 
provided the player has valid reasons to do so, with the difficulty of the
roll upped to {R9{x to {R10{x.  
       
{R1{x  Success    -  {WBright or Pale{x
{R2{x  Successes  -  {WCurrent Primary Emotion{x
{R3{x  Successes  -  {WColor Patterns{x
{R4{x  Successes  -  {WSubtle Shifts{x
{R5+{x Successes  -  {WComplex Mixtures/Patterns{x
          
For details and flair for Role Playing Aura Sight consult our:
{RB{Gi{Wg {ML{Yi{Cs{Rt {Wo{Gf {MA{Wl{Yl {GT{Wh{Ri{Wn{Bg{Ms {YA{Mu{Gr{Ba{x 
             
The vampire may view a particular subject's aura only once with any degree of 
clarity.  Any subsequent attempts that result in failure should be considered 
botches, but after a full month, the character may try again at no penalty.
Finally, and most importantly, just because a kindred can see auras, does not
mean he is granted the knowledge of what they mean.  Colors, Patterns, and
other "tells", must be taught, or discovered by trial and error.
           
{WHack and Slash / Out of Character{x
{WSyntax:  {caura <target>{x
This will read your target's aura.  You will see the intensity of the aura,
as well as the primary color.
~
0 coat baalscaress baals_caress blood_agony bloodagony~

{RBaal's Caress {W/ {RBlood Agony{x
     {RQuietus{x {W****{x
        
A refinement of the blood poisoning of the Scorpion's Touch, Baal's Caress 
allows the vampire to transmute her blood into a virulent ichor that destroys 
any living or undead flesh it touches instead of simply causing weakness.  One 
usually does so by coating a bladed weapon with the blood poison.  It is said
Assamite warriors lick their blades to lubricate them with this foul secretion
as they ride into battle.  Baal's Caress may be used to augment any bladed weapon. 
Everything from poisoned knives and swords to tainted fingernails and claws 
have been reported.
       
{WTable Top / Role Play{x
{WSystem:{x  No roll is necessary to transmute the blood to poison.  The player decides
how many points to transmute and coats any bladed weapon.  The blood-poison is 
sticky and highly concentrated like a thick black sap; it can be used to coat an
arrow head, claws and fingernails.  For as long as the blade is coated the weapon's
damage becomes aggravated.  Every successful strike, even if it inflicts no damage
because of soak with Fortitude, expends one blood point from the total coated weapon.
Therefore it is in the best interest of a warrior to coat a sword or knife with a
goodly amount of blood.  If the attacker misses outright no blood-poison is spent.
      
{WHack and Slash / Out Of Character{x
{WSyntax:  {ccoat <weapon>{x
Using this power on a weapon, adds the aggravated damage type for a limited time.
This also adds a slight damage buff to the weapon.
     
See also: Assamite Quietus
~
0 bloodcurse dagonscall dagons_call~

{RDagon's Call{x
     {RQuietus{x {W***{x
                
With but a touch, the skilled Quietus user can turn her victim's own blood 
against him.  By concentrating, the vampire bursts her target's blood vessels 
and fills his lungs with vitae that proceeds to strangle him from within.  The 
blood actually constricts the target's body from the inside as it floods 
through his system so it works even on unbreathing Cainites.  Until the target 
collapses in agony or the throes of death, this power has no visible effect.
      
{WTable Top / Role Play{x
The vampire must touch her target prior to using Dagon's Call.  Within an hour
thereafter, she may issue the call, though she not need be in the presence or
even in the line of sight of her target.
       
{WSystem:{x Invoking the power costs one Temporary Willpower Point
            {WAttacker Rolls:{x Victim's Stamina {WDiff:{x Opponent Current WP
        {WDefender Rolls:{x Stamina {WDiff:{x Oppnent Current WP
             
The number of successes the attacking player achieves is the number of levels of
lethal damage the victim suffers.  These levels cannot be soaked.  For an additional
Temporary Willpower Points spent in the next turn, the attacker may continue using
Dagon's Call by engaging in another contested Stamina roll.  As long as the player
continues to spend Willpower they may continue rending her opponent from within.
   
{WHack and Slash / Out of Character{x
{WSyntax:{c  bloodcurse <target>{x
This power curses vampires only.  While in effect, the victim cannot make use of
vitae in any manner.  This includes disciplines that require blood to activate,
regeneration, and bloodbuff.  Mobs cannot use special programs that are {rblood{x
fueled in concept (ex. Celerity).
         
See also: Assamite Quietus
~
0 Paradigm~

{CParadigm{x
         
Paradigm is the single most important aspect of creating a Mage character. It is 
the way you believe your magic works, and your conception of reality and the 
universe.  Belief is central to Awakened magic. If you don't believe it can work,
it simply can't.  Defining your paradigm is as simple as stating your character's
belief about how his magic works, what he believes that allows it to work, and what
methods and tools allow him to do so.  A goodly portion of a Mage's paradigm will
be defined by his Tradition.  Some aspects of it will always be personal, however,
and those are the aspects you must define when creating a mage.
       
How deeply you perceive and believe your Paradigm is partly based on your level of
enlightenment (Arete), and partly based on the nature of your character on a 
psychological level.  If your character is not a philosophical sort, or a mystic,
or a spiritual devout, he may not have a great deal of depth to his paradigm until
he grows a great deal through Seekings.
       
{WParadigm Depth{x
       
{CSurface:{x Most common among newly-Awakened mages, this level of depth describes a
         paradigm that is more or less defined as 'this is just how it works,' 
         without much real philosophy behind it.
     
{CShallow:{x Your mage doesn't really think about paradigm much, he just believes it
         on a gut level. He can explain why and how it works in a very sketchy way,
         and he knows some things work better than others for him, but he doesn't 
         spend much time contemplating it.
    
{CStrong:{x  You understand the metaphysics of your paradigm and beliefs well, and have
         tested theory and explored other possibilities.
      
{CDeep:{x    It is rare that a mage reaches this point without a great deal of cosmic 
         awareness (high Arete) and a personality that tends toward delving into
         the mysteries of his personal reality and the universe. It is so much 
         part of the character that it is almost impossible to separate mage and
         paradigm on any conceptual level.
~
0 active becomeactive~

{WActive BecomeActive{x
        
Becoming active allows a player to begin to gain influence in claimable 
domains.  This is done by killing mobs tagged with influence or by role-
play.  Becoming active is irreversable and does carry with it certain
risks.  Other characters might be interested in the domain for themselves.
And just because a domain is claimed, does not guarantee it can be kept.
        
~
