0 rend~

REND THE OSSEOUS FRAME - VICISSITUDE 3
 
This terrible power allows a vampire to manipulate bone in the same manner that 
he shapes flesh.  In conjunction with Transmogrify the Mortal Clay, this power 
enables the Cainite to warp a victim (or himself) beyond recognition.  When 
used alone, it can inflict traumatic injury.  Tzimisce often use this power to 
transform dogs and other beasts into terrible hellhounds and their mortal 
servitors into szlachta, monstrous war-ghouls used to guard havens or strike 
terror into foes on the battlefield.
 
{WSystem{x:  When using this power in conjunction with Transmogrify the Mortal 
Clay, the player makes a Strength + Body Crafts roll (diff 5-9 depending on 
complicated changed)  Cainites who wish to "heal" their alterations must do so 
as if it were aggravated damage.
 
The Cainite may use Rend the Osseous Frame as a weapon. Each success scored on 
the Strength + Body Crafts diff 7 roll inflicts one level of lethal damage to 
the victim as his bones rip, puncture and slice their way out of their skin.  
Vampire victims may soak the lethal damage but their bones are still warped and 
misaligned.  This may cause problems with movement or sight and putting the 
bones back is also treated as healing aggravated wounds.
 
If this power is used on himself to form talons or spikes of bone, the 
recipient takes one level of lethal damage.  If something greater is done such 
as filling the body with quills then the subject takes a number of levels of 
lethal damage equal to 5 minus the number of successes.  (A botch kills a 
mortal subject or sends a vampire into torpor).  This damage to self can be 
healed normally.
 
Knuckle or foot spikes inflict Strength + 2 lethal damage in combat, while 
defensive quills inflict a hand-to-hand attacker's Strength in lethal damage 
unless the attacker scores three or more successes on the attack roll.  (The 
quill-bearing defender still takes damage normally)  The quills also add two to 
all damage rolls for grapples or body slams.
 
The most fearsome attack with this power is the ability to collapse a victim's 
ribcage piercing her heart with her own bones.  This does not send a vampire 
into torpor; it does cause the affected vampire to lose half of her blood 
points. Mortal victims die instantly.  This attack {rmust be declared{x before 
the attack is rolled and it requires 5 successes on the Strength + Body Crafts 
roll to succeed.  The victim still loses the blood points if she soaks all the 
lethal damage.
 
See also:  Tzimisce, Vicissitude
~
0 transmogrify~

TRANSMOGRIFY THE MORTAL CLAY - VICISSITUDE 2
 
This power is similar to Malleable Visage but it allows the Cainite to perform 
drastic, grotesque alterations on other creatures as well as himself.  Only 
flesh (muscle, fat and cartilage) may be transformed.  The power is permanent 
on mortals but vampires may spend blood points to "heal" the transformation.
 
{WSystem{x: The vampire must grapple or restrain the intended victim and the 
player must make a successful Dexterity + Body Crafts roll (dif 5 for a quick 
yank-and-tuck and up to 9 for precise transformations under stressful 
conditions). Increasing another's visage is done under the same as Malleable 
Visage yet the difficulty is reduced to 5.  Vampires who wish to "heal" their 
transformations must spend blood points equal to the total successes.
 
A vampire may use this power to move clumps of skin, fat and muscle to provide 
additional padding where needed.  For each successes on a Dexterity + Body 
Crafts roll (diff 8) the vampire may increase the subject's dice pool for 
soaking attacks by one at the expense of a point of Strength or a health level,
vampire's choice.
 
See also:  Tzimisce, Vicissitude
