0 bloodessence blood_essence~

{RBlood Essence{x
     {RQuietus{x {W*****{x
           
Masters of Quietus have a control over the supernatural properties of vampiric 
vitae that is terrifying to behold.  Blood Essence demonstrates some of the 
most frightening aspects of this control since it clearly illustrates that he 
who controls the blood has access to the unlife of the vampire.  With the power 
an Assamite can distill the unholy life force of a vampire and extract it as a 
thick, blackish blood.  The process is deadly to the victim and very similar to 
Diablerie.  This distilled essence truly is what Cainites refer to as the 
"hearts-blood," the potent vitae that contains all of the vampire's power and 
self.  Once extracted, this mere cupful of blackish liquid contains the entire 
destroyed vampire's essence, and anyone who consumes it effectively diablerizes 
the victim.
 
Blood Essence is an important part of many rituals among the Children of 
Haqim.  Warriors extract the heart's-blood of victims felled in battle and 
bring it back to their elders or even to hidden Alamut itself.  They then 
either consume the essence themselves or present it to an honored teacher.
Assamite sorcerers and viziers are said to have many uses for the heart's-
blood, using it to peel back the layers of a victim's long existence year 
by year.  The essence is also a key component in religious observances among
followers of the {RRoad of Blood{x.
              
     
{WTable Top / Role Play{x
         
The process of distilling the Blood Essence is very similar to diablerie 
itself.  The vampire drains all of his victim's blood through whatever means
are available and then must drain the heart's-blood.  Instead of sucking it 
out through brute force, the vampire uses Quietus to distill the potent vitae.
The vampire's player does not make the extended Strength roll for diablerie.
Instead he makes an extended Willpower roll (diff 9) that functions like the
strength roll causing an unsoakable level of aggy damage per success.  Failure
means the vampire must pause to distill the essence but can continue next turn.
 A botch means the effort fails, though the vampire may proceed to diablerize
in the traditional means.  As in diablerie, the victim remains alert and can
fight back.  Once all health levels are gone, the victim is destroyed and his 
essence is fully drained, usually into a chalice of some sort.  The distilled
heart's-blood remains liquid and fresh for a number of nights equal to the 
Quietus master's Willpower.  After that time it becomes caked and dry and loses
its potency.  Anyone drinking the heart's-blood while it is still fresh gains
all the benefits and potential pitfalls of having successfully diablerized the
victim, such as lowered generation.
        
{WSystem:{x  Willpower {WDiff:{x 9
       
For material related to this power see:
            
