0 agony~

BAAL'S CARESS - QUIETUS 4
 
A refinement of the blood poisoning of the Scorpion's Touch, Baal's Caress 
allows the vampire to transmute her blood into a virulent ichor that destroys 
any living or undead flesh it touches instead of simply causing weakness.  One 
usually does so by coating a bladed weapon with the blood poison, and Cainite 
veterans of the Reconquista and Crusades report stories of the Assamite 
warriors licking their blades to lubricate them with this foul secretion as 
they rode into battle.  Baal's Caress may be used to augment any bladed weapon. 
Everything from poisoned knives and swords to tainted fingernails and claws 
have been reported.
 
{WSystem{x:  No roll is necessary to transmute the blood to poison.  The player 
simply decides how many points to transmute and coats any bladed weapon.  The 
blood-poison is sticky and highly concentrated like a thick black sap; it can 
be used to coat an arrow head, claws and fingernails.  For as long as the blade 
is coated the weapon's damage becomes aggravated.  Every successful strike 
({reven if it inflicts no damage because of soak with Fortitude{x) expends one 
blood point from the total coated weapon.  Therefore it is in the best interest 
of a warrior to coat a sword or knife with a goodly amount of blood.  If the 
attacker misses outright no blood-poison is spent.
 
See also:  Quietus, Assamite
~
0 dagon~

DAGON'S CALL - QUIETUS 3
 
With but a touch, the skilled Quietus user can turn her victim's own blood 
against him.  By concentrating, the vampire bursts her target's blood vessels 
and fills his lungs with vitae that proceeds to strangle him from within.  The 
blood actually constricts the target's body from the inside as it floods 
through his system so it works even on unbreathing Cainites.  Until the target 
collapses in agony or the throes of death, this power has no visible effect.
 
{WSystem{x:  The vampire must touch her target prior to using Dagon's Call.  
Within an hour thereafter, she may issue the call, though she not need be in 
the presence or even in the line of sight of her target.  Invoking the power 
costs one Willpower point. The player then makes a resisted Stamina roll 
against the target's Stamina; the difficulty of each roll is equal to the 
opponent's Willpower. The number of successes the attacking player achieves is 
the number of levels of lethal damage the victim suffers.  These levels 
{rcannot{x be soaked.  For an additional Willpower spent in the next turn, the 
player may continue using Dagon's Call by engaging in another contested Stamina 
roll.  As long as the player continues to spend Willpower they may continue 
rending her opponent from within.
 
See Also:  Quietus, Assamite
