0 silenceoffieryblood silenceofdeath~

{RSilence of Fiery Blood{x
     {RQuietus{x {W*{x
        
Warriors and lovers both know the sensory effects of fiery blood.  In the midst 
of battle or passion, all extraneous sounds fall away and one is only focused 
on the enemy or the partner.  For Assamites, this state is second nature.  
Warriors use it in battle, viziers and sorcerers in study.  With the 
blood-power of Quietus, however, they can make it manifest in the very world 
around them.  All things around them fade into silence - for the Assamite and 
everyone else. Although sounds from beyond the immediate area can and do filter 
through, nothing in the immediate vicinity can emit even a peep.  Be it a 
victim's screams, a loud crash or a lover's moan.  It all fades into 
nothingness. In most cases, this nimbus moves with the vampire but it is 
possible to infuse a specific location with the Silence of Fiery Blood.
         
{WTable Top / Role Play
{WSystem:{x  No roll is necessary but the power costs one blood point and one action
No roll is necessary but the power costs one blood point and one standard action
to activate for the common version.  This zone of silence has a radius of 20 feet.
No sound occurs inside this zone however noises from without can be heard.  This
zone remains in affect following the vampire until she wills it to stop.
           
The second application is called the Curse of Silence.  The character spends 
two blood points and spends five turns in concentration in a room or 
enclosure.  Like the common version, the silence zone is 20 feet but will 
remain within the room until the vampire wishes it to cease.  The vampire can 
leave the room and the silence will remain lasting through day or night.  A 
vampire can only create one zone of silence at a time, attempting to create a 
second will cause the first to fade automatically.
             
{WHack and Slash / Out of Character{x
{WSyntax:  {csilenceofdeath{x
At the cost of blood, the user of Silence will be able to sneak.  Additionally,
no sound/speech based abilities may be used in the same room (user, teammates,
nor mobs).  This will stop prayers, certain Disciplines, as well as voice
dependent mob special programs (such as Dominate-based).
 
See also: Assamite Quietus
~
