0 banking banks deposit withdrawal balance~

{DBanking{x
             
Banks serve a variety of purposes, the most obvious being a place for characters
to store their excess money without having to purchase large amounts of jewels
or precious metals from a jeweler, which in turn frees up inventory space.  Any 
currency deposited into the banking system accumulates interest.  Interest is
calculated on the amount in the account and the Resources Background.  
Additionally those who control a domain will have profits from that domain
deposited into their account regularly.
          
Organizations also have accounts for the various Tribes, Clans, and Traditions, 
and members are able to make deposits, to help fund financial endevours.  The 
head of that organization is the only person that can make withdrawls initially, 
but can give this option to others, depending on the structure of the organ-
ization and it's policies.
          
Banks throughout the world are connected, and your account can be accessed from
any of them.  You must be inside the bank for the following commands to function.
              
{WSyntax:  {cbank/clanbank withdraw #{x     Withdraw # in Gold.
{W         {cbank/clanbank deposit #{x      Deposit # in Gold.
{W         {cbank/clanbank balance{x        Display current balance.
{W         {cbank/clanbank{x                Display banking options.
     
See also:  {WWorth Resources Domain Economy Inventory{x
~
0 bloodbuff~

Vampires, even those without the physical disciplines of Potence,
Fortitude and Celerity can still increase their physical prowess merely
by willing it.  Vitae can be spent to increase a vampire's physical
stats, temporarily giving them the ability to hit harder in combat,
and increase her durability overall.
{x
This will increase your Strength, Dexterity, and Stamina all by 1 for a
short time.  Once buffed, it cannot be stacked upon itself.  Ghouls may
also take advantage of this ability.
 
Syntax: {cbloodbuff{x
 
See also:  VAMPIRE POTENCE CELERITY FORTITUDE
