0 earthmeld~

{REarthmeld{x
{R        Protean {W***{x
 
Syntax:  {cearthmeld{x
 
One of the most prized abilities given by Protean, Earth Meld enables a
vampire to become one with the earth.  She literally sinks into the bare
ground, transmuting her substance to bond with the earth.  While interred,
she cannot move, but becomes undetectable and immune to sunlight.
 
{WTable Top / Role Play{x
{WSystem:{x  The vampire spends a blood point, and takes a turn to meld into
the earth.  She is one step away from Torpor at this point, and must make a
Humanity roll (diff 6) to rouse in response to danger prior to her desired
time of emergence.
 
{WOut of Character / Hack and Slash{x
{WSystem:  {xBy spending blood, the vampire will meld into the earth.  While
melding, she is immune to being attacked, and immune to sunlight.  Using any
physical command will pop her up from the ground.  Earthmeld can only be used
on bare ground, it cannot be used in the city, in the air, over water, etc.
 
{WSee Also:  Protean{x
~
0 claws talonsofthebeast talons_of_the_beast~

{RTalons of the Beast{x
{R        Protean {W**{x
 
{WSyntax:{c  claws{x

A Cainite with Talons of the Beast can extrude wicked claws a few inches long 
from each fingertip.  Despite the powers name, the claws are far more dangerous 
than those of a mere wolf or bear.  They can tear through chain armor and still 
dig deep into flesh.  Wounds inflicted upon mortals by the Talons of the Beast 
never quite heal; Cainites find that vitae alone is insufficient to heal them. 
Some vampires exhibit other minor changes when activating this power. Eyes 
might turn a chalky white, blood might seep from the palms, or the character 
might be unable to keep his fangs retracted.
 
{WTable Top / Role Play{x
{WSystem:  {xActivating the Discipline is a free action, but it takes a full turn
to take effect, and the player must spend one blood point.  Wounds inflicted by 
the Talons of the Beast do Strength +1 dice of aggravated damage.
 
{WHack and Slash / Out of Character{x
{WSystem:  {xThe player spends 1 blood point to grow claws.  When unarmed, the claws
provide bonus damage, as well as dealing slashing-type damage.  You may wield
a weapon while claws are out, but doing so will negate the bonuses while armed.

See also:  {WProtean Gangrel{x
~
0 gleamoftheredeye~

{RGleam of the Red Eye{x
{R        Protean {W*{x
 
Syntax:  {cgleam{x

The vampire with this ability can see normally in ordinary darkness.  Even a 
cloudy, moonless night is as bright as an overcast day to the character.  
However, the discipline does cause the characters eyes to glow a visible red, 
which unnerves most mortals who see it.
 
{WTable Top / Role Play{x
{WSystem:  {xActivating this Discipline is a free action, but it takes a full turn
to take effect.  While it is in effect, the vampire suffers no dice pool penalties
based on ordinary darkness.  However, while active, the character suffers a +1
difficulty to all Social rolls due to her red eyes.
 
{WOut of Character / Hack and Slash{x
{WSystem:  {xWhile Gleam is active, you are granted Darkvision.  Additionally, your
Charisma and Manipulation are both reduced by 1.
 
{WSee Also:  Protean{x
~
0 majesty~

{RMajesty{x
     {RPresence{x {W*****{x
    
Upon the activation of this power, the vampire becomes universally respected
and/or feared.  It is as if what those affected, somewhat forget what their usual 
opinion or attitude is towards the now, Magestic vampire.  They are likely to
treat the user, respectfully and without conscious thought.  Indeed, at the very
sight of the Canite, jaws to drop in awe and even the most courageous cower. 
It simply seems the kindred is so formidable that no one would even consider
crossing them, let alone making a physical challenge.  This power stops others
from attacking or harming the vampire in any way for as long as the affects 
remain unresisted.
      
{WTable Top / Role Play{x
{WSystem:{x  No roll is neccessary for the user to activate Majesty.  However, anyone
near the user must roll Courage (Difficulty of the vampire's Charisma + Intimidation).
A subject who fails the roll will go to absurd lengths to humble herself before the
vampire.  Kindred may spend a point of Willpower to overcome such feelings if the roll
is failed.  Either way, this process is repeated each turn they victim is in the
vampires vicinity.
           
{WHack and Slash / Out of Character{x
{WSyntax:  {cmajesty{x
This highest power of the Presence discipline makes the vampire the object of
fear and respect.  Simply put, aggressive mobiles will not attack the kindred.
This power rerquires a point of Willpower to be spent.
 
See also: Presence
~
0 entrancement~

{REntrancement{x
     {RPresence{x {W***{x
       
Entrancement is used to convince another to serve you.  The subject becomes 
enchanted and desires to serve your needs.  But, unlike a person under Dominate
powers, the subject of Entrancement retains their freedom of action and creativity. 
This is emotional manipulation instead of mental control.  In many ways
this is similar to a Blood Bond, with the loyalty and devotion obtained springing
from the thrall's emotions, the vitcim wanting to please the vampire.  This is not 
precise, and victims tend to express themselves to the Canite in unexpected ways.
       
{WTable Top / Role Play{x
{WSystem:{x  Manipulation + Empathy {WDiff:{x Target Permanent Willpower 
The number of successes determines how long the victim is Entranced.  There is not a 
way to extend a period of Entrancement, and once the condition wears off, the victim 
is likely to think ill of the vampire.            
           
{R1{x  success    -  {WOne Hour{x
{R2{x  successes  -  {WOne Day{x
{R3{x  successes  -  {WOne Week{x
{R4{x  successes  -  {WOne Month{x
{R5+{x successes  -  {WOne Year{x
          
{WOut of Character / Hack and Slash{x
{WSyntax:  {centrance <target> <action>{x
Entrancement allows the vampire to give a one word or brief command to a
mobile.  There are many applications to this power in the game.  You will
have to experiment to see what is possible.
 
See also:  Presence
~
0 dreadgaze~

{RDread Gaze{x
{R        Presence {W**{x
 
The exhibition of your full vampiric powers can cause great fear and loathing 
in mortals. This is usually accomplished by baring teeth and claws while 
hissing loudly. While most vampires can performing this action, you are 
exceptionally adept at it, and are capable of driving mortals insane with fear, 
or frightening them into submission or flight with the merest snarl. The 
subjects are cowed by your appearance and will do anything to avoid incurring 
your wrath.
 
{WTable Top / Role Play{x
{WSystem:{x The player must roll Charisma + Intimidation (difficulty is the 
victim's Wits + Courage). Any success indicates that the target is cowed, while 
three or more successes indicate that he runs away in fear. Moreover, each 
success reduces the number of dice the victim is allowed to roll the next turn 
by one.
 
This roll may be attempted only once per turn, though if performed in 
successive turns, the vampire may collect successes as an extended roll in 
order to completely subjugate the target. Eventually the target may lose so 
many dice that he will be unable to do anything but curl up on the ground and 
weep. Failure indicates that the attempt has faltered. All collected successes 
are lost, the victim may act normally again and the player must start over next 
turn. A botch indicates the victim is not at all impressed, and any use of 
Presence by the character will not be effective against him again this session.
 
{WOut of Character / Hack and Slash{x
{WSyntax: {cdreadgaze <target>{x
On a successful roll, your target becomes terrified and flees from combat.

See also:  Presence Brujah Toreador Ventrue
~
1 awe~

{RAwe{x
{R        Presence {W*{x
 
When you employ this power, everyone near you becomes intensely attracted to 
you. They will do nearly anything to be close to you, although their 
fascination is not so complete that they will endanger themselves. The effects 
last only as long as the subjects are in your presence, but the next time they 
see you, the feelings are likely to be reawakened.
 
By carefully using this power, you can have phenomenal powers of mass 
communication. Since Presence uses emotions to sway victims, it doesn't really 
matter what is said; but you can more easily convince people of a certain 
course of action or the nobility of a purpose by using this Discipline.
 
{WTable Top / Role Play{x
{WSystem:{x The player must roll Charisma + Expression (difficulty of 7). Those 
affected can us Willpower points to overcome the effect, but must continue 
spending Willpower every few minutes for as long as they remain in the same 
area as the character. However, a soon as a number of Willpower equivalent to 
the number of successes rolled is spent, the Awe is completely shaken off, and 
the subject can't be affected for the rest of the scene.
 
The number of successes rolled also determines how many people can be affected: 
1 Success - one person
2 Successes - two people
3 Successes - six people
4 Successes - 20 people
5 Successes - everyone in the vampire's immediate vicinity
 
{WOut of Character / Hack and Slash{x
{WSyntax:  {cawe{x
With a successful Charisma + Expression roll, all npcs/mobs in the room
become awed.  Awed shopkeepers look favorably upon you, and awed enemies
have a harder time landing an attack on you.  You can see your current
list of awed mobs in your {yaffect{x screen.
 
See Also:  {WPresence Brujah Toreador Ventrue{x
~
1 shadowform tenebrous body~

{RTenebrous Body{x {W|{x {RShadow Form{x 
     {RObtenebration{x {W*****{x
             
At this level, the Kindred's mastery of darkness is so extensive that she
may physically change into it.   This darkness is not merely the absence
of light, but is the essence of the Abyss.  Vampires in this form are 
practically invulnerable and may slither through cracks and crevices.  
Additionally, the vampire gains the ability to see in utter darkness.
               
The form the individual takes when becoming darkness, is unique, each a
representation of the mind and soul of the vampire, and is generally,
the same, each time this power is used.  This power is gravely super-
natural, and generally causes terror in those who witness it.
        
{WTable Top / Role Play{x
      
{WSystem:{x No roll is needed to activate this power.  The character spends
        {R3{x {WBlood Points{x over the course of {R3{x {WTurns{x, the 
transformation complete at the beginning of the next round.  
 
The vampire is immune to physical attack while in the tenebrous form, though she
still takes aggravated damage from fire and sunlight.   By the same token, the 
vampire cannot physically attack, or manipulate tangable things.  They may, 
however, envelop and ooze over others, affecting them in the same manner as 
Shroud of Night, and may use mental disciplines.  The vampire can slither up
walls and across ceilings or "drip" darkness upward,  they have no mass and
are thus unaffected by gravity.  The Rotschreck Difficulty Roll applied to
Fire and Sunlight,increase by one for vampires in this form, as the light is
even more painful to their shadowy bodies.
                  
Those not accustomed to such displays, and witness such a transformation into 
this unholy shadow must succeed on the following roll or suffer from 
debilitating terror.
         
{WSystem:{x Courage {WDiff:{R 8{x 
           
{WHack and Slash / Out of Character{x
{WSyntax:  {cshadowform{x
When taking the Tenebrous Form, the vampire becomes living intangeble darkness.
In game terms, he becomes impervious to physical attack.  Conversly, the vampire
can't deal out damage of any kind  and the affects of fire and sunlight are 
doubled.  Additionally The kindred may pass through closed doors and gains hide
and dark vision.     
    
~
1 nightshade black metamorphisis~

{RBlack Metamorphosis{x {W|{x {RNight Shades{x
{R        Obtenebration {W****{x
      
The Lasombra calls upon his inner darkness and infuses himself with it, 
becoming a monstrous hybrid of matter and shadow.  His body becomes 
mottled with spots of tenebrous shade, and wispy tentacles extrude from
his torso and abdomen.  Though still humanoid, the Lasombra takes on an
almost demonic appearance, as the darkness summoned from the abyss,
to the surface.
          
{WTable Top / Role Play{x
{WSystem:{x  Player spends {R2{x {WBlood Points{x, and then rolls:
         {WSystem:{x Manipulation + Courage {WDiff:{R 7{x
       
Failure indicates the vampire cannot undergo the Black Metamorphosis, and the 
{R2{x {WBP's{x are spent nontheless.  Botching inflicts {r2{x Unsoakable health levels of
lethal damage on the vampire, as the abyss ravages his undead body.
                     
While affected with Black Metamorphosis, the vampire possesses four tentacles
similar to those created with Arms of the Abyss, with the exception, these
Arm's have Strength and Dexterity ratings equal to the kindred's own.  
In Combat, this power truely shines, and active users, subtract {R2{x {WDice{x
from a victim's: {WStamina{x and {WSoak{x  Dicepools, if the victims is
physically touched in combat, and this effect lasts as long as the vampire
remains in contact with the victim.  The tentacles are then able to make an
additional attack, as the four arms ravage the victim in unison.  Many 
Lasombra cultivate this power and it's devilish aspect, simply because it
adds {R3{x Dice to the Kindred's {WIntimidation{x Dice Pools.  Sometimes,
overlooked, and quite useful, is the vampire can now see in pitch darkness.
    
At this level of Obtenebration,  the vampire is truely tied to the Abyss,
and the darkness produced at this level is blatantly supernatural. Those not
accustomed to such displays, and witness such black horror, must succeed on
the following roll or suffer from debilitating terror.
     
{WSystem:{x Courage {WDiff:{R 8{x
         
