1 shroudofnight~

{RShroud of Night{x
{R        Obtenebration {W**{x
        
The vampire can create a cloud of inky blackness that completely obscures 
light and even sound to some extent.  Those who have been trapped within
this power describe it as viscous and unnerving.  This manifestation lends
credence to the tales  that claim  Obtenebrational darkness is something
more than mere shadow.  Once summoned the Shroud can be commanded to move,
but this requires complete concentraion on the part of the vampire.    
       
{WTable Top / Role Play{x
{WSystem:{x Manipulation + Occult  {WDiff:{x {R7{x
One Success generates darkness roughly {R10{x feet in diamater, which constantly
shifts and undulates, at times even extending shadowy tendrils.  Each additional
success doubles the diameter of the cloud, though the vampire may voluntarily 
reduce the area she wishes to cover.  The cloud may be invoked at a distance of
up to {R50{x yards, but invoking this power outside the vampire's line of sight
adds {R2{x to the Difficulty, and also requires the vampire to spend {R1 BP{x.
 
The shadow mass will extinguish light sources it engulfs, with the exception of
open flame, and muffles sounds to the point of indistinguishability. Those within
lose all sense of sight and feel as though they've been immersed in a black void,
and adds blindness and darkness penalties to appropriate Actions.  Even those
who have some recourse in this situation, such as Heightened Senses, Feral Sight,
and Mage Perceptions, still suffer {R+2{x Difficulty on such such dice rolls. 
This experience can be very tramatic, and reduces all {WStamina{x based dicepools
by {R2{x Dice.  This penalty is not cumulative with that of Shadow Play.  Finally,
those unaccustomed to such a display must succeed on a Courage roll (Diff: 8)
or flee in panic.  
          
{WHack and Slash / Out of Character{x
{WSyntax:{c  shroud{x
Activating this power drops an area of darkness into the room, lowering
Stamina of all mobs in the room, and potentially blinding them.  This
costs blood to activate.
 
See also: Obtenebration Lasombra
~
1 shadowplay~

{RShadow Play{x
     {RObtenebration{x {W*{x
               
This power grants the vampire a limited control over shadows and other ambient 
darkness.  Though the vampire cannot truly "create" darkness, she can overlap 
and stretch existing shadows, creating patches of gloom.  This power also
allows Kindred to separate the shadow from their body, and even shape darkness 
into phantasms that are not truly there.  Gaining a mystical tangibility under
the vampire's manipulation, this shadow stuff can vary from freezing cold to 
hellishly hot, and can be used to aggravate or even smother victims.  
Certain callous Lasombra claim to have choked mortals to death with their
own shadows.
          
{WTable Top / Role Play{x
{WSystem:{x No roll is needed, but the vampire must burn {R1{x {WBlood Point{x
         to activate this effect. It does not requrie active concentraion, 
 and it lasts for the duration of the scene, or until it is dismissed.
 the Canite dismisses it, and can be used various ways. 
           
{RAs a Cloak:{x
{R+1{x die to any roll involving Stealth. 
{R+1{x Difficulty to Ranged Attacks against user.
   
{RTo Frighten or Intimidate:{x 
{R+1{x die to any roll involving Intimidation.  
{R-1{x die to any roll using Soak or Stamina.
     
Mortals, those that still breath, that are reduced to {R0{x Stamina in this
manner begin to asphyxiate, while vampires lose all appropriate dice but are
otherwise unaffected.  When using Shadow Play to frighten or intimidate, only
one subject may be affected by this power at a time.  This effect is extremely
disconcerting, and those unaccustomed to such a display must gain at least one
success on a Courage roll (Diff: 8), or all Dice Pools are reduced by {R1{x die
for the remainder of the current scene.
      
{WHack and Slash / Out of Character{x
{WSyntax:  {cshadowplay <target>{x
When used with no target, you bolster your own stealth and intimidation.  All
d10 rolls requiring either Stealth or Intimidation gain +1 to the dicepool
while you are affected by your own shadows.  When targeting an enemy, your
shadows suffocate the target, giving a -1 to their Stamina.  For higher rolls,
immediate damage as well as blindness can occur.  Additionally, while a target
is affected by your shadowplay, they receive suffocation damage throughout the
fight, as long as the target has lungs to be suffocated.  This does mean that
certain entities will be immune to the ongoing damage (vampires, constructs,
spirits, wraiths, and others).  The attack roll is based upon Wits + Obtenebration.
See also: Obtenebration Lasombra Abyss
~
