-1 WAYLAY~

Waylay is a skill most commonly used by bandits and mercenaries.  By surprising 
their enemy, these classes can get an extra round of attack before their 
opponent has a chance to react with their own offensive maneuver. Because the 
element of surprise is so vital to this skill, it is impossible to use it in 
the middle of combat. 
 
Extra Note: We of Haven of the Embraced would like to thank Fotito and 
Nevermore for the idea of this skill. It was created as a gift for them after 
they completed a quest. 
 
Also help on: MERCENARIES BANDITS SKILLS 
~
-1 knights-renown~

RENOWN
Perfected only by knights, renown is the ability to take less damage from 
physical attacks.  After many years of study, knights grow accustomed to the 
damage they take in combat, and lessen its affects on their body and armour.  
By using this skill, knights can take the brunt of an attack for a much longer 
period of time than they would be able to otherwise.

Also help on: KNIGHTS KNIGHT's TRAINING SKILLS
~
-1 knights-training~

KNIGHT'S TRAINING
Knights are the most extensively trained class in the art of combat.  As the 
clergy spend hours upon hours perfecting their prayers, so do the knights 
practice their abilities in combat. Because of this extra training their form 
in combat is far superior to others and they are able to inflict extra damage.

Also help on: KNIGHTS RENOWN SKILLS
~
-1 OOCS~

OOCs
Haven of the Embraced is not a roleplaying enforced mud.  Because of this, some 
of the conversation that goes on is OOC or out of character.  In fact,  one of
the most used channels on the MUD is our ooc channel. It can be used by typing 
ooc (then what it is you wish for the whole mud to see).  Any sort of 
conversation is allowed to go be held over this channel.  However, Haven of the 
Embraced is a PG13-rated MUD and we ask all of our members to follow the 
guideline and not heavily swear over public channels.

Also help on: CHANNELS GOSSIP MUSIC TELLS SHOUT YELL CLAN_CHANNEL SECTS_CHANNEL 
QUESTION ANSWER SAY OSAY IC
~
