0 quest_points qp~

{WQUEST POINTS {D({WQP{D){x

Quest Points are an Out-Of-Character (OOC) form of currency that can be earned
in a multitude of ways on Haven.  These Quest Points (commonly referred to as
QP for short), can be spent to increase your character's capabilities in the game.

------------------------------------------------------
QP may be earned in several ways:
*Killing enemies
*Roleplaying with others ({CIC{x)
*As a reward for Immortal Run quests
*By exchanging unneeded tomes to Meric
------------------------------------------------------
QP may be spent on the following:
*Purchasing Quest Equipment (QEQ)
*Purchasing Levels
*Used when setting a new {yHometown{x
*Restringing equipment ({rRequires an Immortal assist{x)
------------------------------------------------------

You are able to use the {yquest{x command to purchase your own quest equipment,
or gift levels to yourself or others.

{yQuest List{x will show you the QEQ list and prices.
{yQuest Buy Itemname{x will allow you to purchase the QEQ piece.
{yQuest Level #{x will allow you to purchase # levels for yourself.
{yQuest Gift Personname #{x will allow you to gift # levels to another.

Levels and {Crestrings{x may be purchased for 100 QP each.

{WSee Also:  IC OOC RESTRINGS HOMETOWN{x
~
-1 SLIP~

SLIP
Slip is a trickster only ability that requires quite a bit of skill to use. It 
momentarily confuses the opponent as the character using it goes into hiding.
However, the move is hard to perfect and takes a bit of time to perform. 
Therefore, to be able to surprise an opponent before they are able to attack 
again, it is helpful to have them blinded.  This makes dirt kicking a very 
valuable skill.

Also help on: DIRT KICKING BLAST
~
0 blast~

{yBlast{x
{y    Legardemain {W****{x

{WSyntax: {cblast <target>{x

Roguish characters have mastered the art of misdirection, using this skill to
great advantage, even in combat.  With a bit of trickery, you can emit a small
amount of smoke and flame at the target, dealing a moderate amount of fire
damage, as well as having a chance of blinding the target.
 
{WTable Top / Role Play{x
{WSystem:{x  The character using trickery and misdirection to discretely use a
combination of flash powder and tinder, creating a brief blast of smoke and
flame, directed at the opponent's face.  A Dexterity + Legardemain Roll
(difficulty 6) is required.  The target takes fire damage equal to the number
of successes, soakable as applicable.  On a successful hit, the target makes
a Wits + Alertness Roll (difficulty 3 + Character's Legardemain), failure
leaves the target blinded by the smoke and flame for two turns.
 
{WHack and Slash / Out of Character:{x
{WSystem:  {xThis skill requires the usage of 'blast powder' to activate.  This
attack is considered fire damage, and has the chance to fireblind your target.
~
-1 FORTIFY~

FORTIFY
To make their ability to sustain damage even greater, Guards have the special 
ability to make their shields stronger. This skill, fortify, increases the 
defense on shields depending on the guards skill and level. It proves to be a 
valuable tool in combat for the Guardsmen.

~
-1 STUDY~

STUDY
Study is the ability to learn things about the world. In particular, it tells 
which components are used to make up different types of potions.  Because 
potions are becoming increasingly rare in the world, this skill along with brew 
are vital to a character's success and wealth.

{RCurrently Disabled{x

Also help on: BREW
~
0 brewing~

{yBrew{x
{y        Hearth Wisdom {D**{x
{W        (Requires a mixing pot, an empty vial, ingredients){x

Brew is the ability to make potions.  It requires a mixing pot, some glass 
vials, and the correct components to successfully make a potion.  To determine
what components are needed for different potions, the study skill can be used. 
With the increase in price of potions, the combination of the study and brew 
skill are very important.

{WSystem:{x  Roll Intelligence + Hearth Wisdom (difficulty: potion level + 3)
{WSyntax:  {cbrew{x
{c         brew <potion>{x

{cBrew{x by itself will show potions you can make.  Upon being able to brew, you
can increase the Secondary Ability 'Brewing' with Freebies.  Higher levels
of Brewing give access to more potions.
{R*{WStatus: Testing{x
 
Also help on: STUDY
~
-1 SKIN~

SKIN
Skin is a skill granted to all players.  Using it, a character is able to 
remove the skin off of a corpse that has recently fallen.  These skins can then
be sold at the general store and will eventually be able to be used in the 
crafting of certain types of armor. It is a very interesting skill that will 
prove to be very useful.

Also help on: SKILL
~
-1 HEADBUTT~

HEADBUTT
Headbutt is a very useful skill that can only be used by bandits.  Their rough 
fighting has taught them how to use their heads in combat to attempt to gain an
advantage.  While the headbutt does not do a lot of damage on its own, an 
exceptional headbutt will in fact render an opponent temporarily unconscious. 
While the target is out cold, the bandit could land a surprise attack, attempt 
to heal and regroup, or easily escape.

~
-1 builders~

Builders are very important to the improvement of Haven without builders in the
past, none of the areas and mobs on Haven would exist at all. The Admins are
always looking for talented builders to help add to the world and enrich the
playing experience for the players.
{x
If you are interested in becoming a builder for Haven there are a few steps you 
must take. The first is to play the game. Builders for Haven must have at least 
two weeks experience on the game to get an idea of some of the other areas and 
how new areas could fit into the theme and setting of Haven. After that, fill 
out the "Immortal Application" listed under '{chelp immortal_application{x' and 
either note it to Immortal or email it to one of the Admins. With the 
application, you'll be asked to send a sample of some room, mob, and object
descriptions and an area concept for your first area. Send all of that and one 
of the Admins will contact you within a few days.
{x
See also help: immortal_application, immortal, imms_list, contact
~
0 remort~

Remorting allows a player to reduce his/her level back to level one and become 
more powerful overall.  You must be level 100 in order to remort.  When remorting,
a character keeps his or her character sheet stats, skills, percentages increased,
as well as equipment and money earned.  The character's hit points, mana, movement,
and experience to level are all reset to level 1 values.  Every remort increases
your experience to level.
 
Syntax:  {yremort {x<{yargument{x>

Remort options are:
<no argument> (any)               - Gain 3 Freebies
garou (human only)                - Changes you into a {GGarou{Y*{x
rank (garou only)                 - Increases a Garou's Rank
mage <tradition>{B**{x (human only)   - Changes you into a {CMage{Y*{x
 
{Y*{xRemorting {GGarou{D/{CMage{x also gives you 3 Freebies
{Y*{xAdditionally, you will need to redo your character sheet.
{B**{xRemorting {CMage{x requires you to set your Tradition during Remort.
{B**{x<tradition> needs to be the proper name of the Tradition, or first word

Examples: 
{yremort{x
{yremort garou{x
{yremort mage order{x
{yremort mage akashic{x
 
See Also:  {WGarou Vampire Mage Freebie Rank Tradition{x
~
