-1 TRADITIONS~

{CTraditions{x
      
The Traditions (formally called the Nine Mystic Traditions) are an alliance of
secret societies that exist to unify users of magic under a common banner to 
preserve magick and protect reality (particularly those parts of reality that 
are magical) from unstable mages such as Marauders and Nephandi. Each of the
Traditions are largely independent organizations unified by a broadly accepted
paradigm for practicing magic. The Traditions themselves vary substantially from
one another. Some have almost no structure or rules, while others have rigid rules
of protocol, etiquette, and rank. Though unified in their desire to keep magic 
alive, the magicks practiced by different Traditions are often wildly different
and entirely incompatible with one another. Understanding Traditions as a whole
requires understanding each Tradition separately, and then assembling them into
a somewhat cohesive whole. 
             
Although there are nine traditions in the Mage: The Ascension Line, Haven
supports the following five:
   
{WSyntax:{x Help {C<Tradition Name>{x   
       
Akashic Brotherhood        Help {CAkashic{x
Dreamspeakers              Help {CDreamSpeaker{x
Euthanatos                 Help {CEuthanatos{x
Order of Hermes            Help {CHermes{x
Verbena                    Help {CVerbena{x
         
Additonal Information related to the Traditions can be found here:
       
{WSyntax:{x Help {C<Topic>{x
    
Help {CSpheres{x
Help {CParadigm{x
Help {CMagick{x
Help {CMage{x
