-1 SPHERES~

{CSpheres{x
            
Magick is divided into nine Spheres. These Spheres are more like schools of 
thought or religions than any form of discipline. To invoke a Magickal effect
a Mage must believe whole-heartedly in a set of theories and concepts.  For 
example, no one believes that a normal, everyday human can walk on water. But
a Mage trained in Matter can believe that the presence of an awakened Avatar
alters the laws of surface tension to allow the water to harden near to that 
of a solid.  The Spheres of magick are named based on the properties they most
alter in reality. There are some laws of existence that don't fit within these
nine Spheres, so some Mages believe that there must be a tenth Sphere that has
yet to be discovered.
       
Details on each Sphere are found in the following Help Topics:
        
{WSyntax:{x Help {C<Sphere Name>{x
        
Help {CCorrespondence{x   
Help {CEntropy{x
Help {CForces{x
Help {CLife{x
Help {CMatter{x
