-1 AVATAR~

{CAvatar{x
      
The Avatar is the source of an Awakened individual's ability to perform magic,
and which grants the possibility of Ascension.  Mages experience the Avatar as
a separate personality which is connected to the mage's soul, and which drives
the mage toward Ascension. It will often speak to the mage, as a "voice in the
head" or via dreams. Avatars generally take on a humanoid form of the opposite
gender to the mage, though this is not always the case and is highly dependent
on the mage's interpretation. Avatars are also in control of a mage's Seekings.
     
Avatars were historically guided to their mages by spirits known as psychopomps.
The presence of psychopomps was direct result of the appearance of the Entelechy,
and they radiated forward and backward in time from that point. During this time
(which includes the Dark Ages), psychopomps chose mages and Avatars so perfectly
matched that many mages were completely unaware of the presence of the Avatar,
referring to it only as a sort of mystical Fount of energy. Unfortunately, this
often meant the inner voice of the Avatar was rendered silent, and mages were free
to pursue their own petty personal agendas. However, as time progressed away from
the Entelechy, psychopomps become less common, leaving it up to Avatars to find
their own mages.
    
While some mages see Avatars as extra-dimensional entities, others see them as
facets of a greater consciousness, or even of the Tapestry itself. Along these
lines, the Traditions often teach that Avatars are soul-shards of the "Pure Ones",
ancient mages who Ascended long ago and who now seek to aid modern mages.
       
Each Avatar has an Essence, that describes the Avatar's nature, as well as the
way in which the Avatar seeks Ascension. An Avatar's Essence usually, though not
always, complements the mage's own desires and outlook on magic and life.
      
{WThe four major Essences are:{x
       
    {CDynamic{x    - Growth through change and freedom.
    {CPattern{x    - Strength through order and structure.
    {CPrimordial{x - Improvement through purification.
    {CQuesting{x   - Striving for balance and purpose.
   
     
Avatar affects a wide range of magickal effects but in general effects how
fast the Mage regenerates Quintessence and how long his affects last.
      
Freebie Cost:  7 * Current Level 
       
{WWARNING: {CRaising your Arete to level {W5 {Cwill 'lock' your Avatar rating
         to its current variable.{x
 
~
-1 ARETE~

{CArete{x
                
Arete is a measure of how much the mage understands reality. A mage with high
Arete understands how reality works, how it influences him, how he influences 
reality and himself. He will see how he and the world reflect each other. A mage
with low arete doesn't understand how everything connects together, and is filled
with the same illusions as most sleepers. As he increases his understanding, he 
will comprehend more and more of reality, thus gaining power over it.
            
The spheres of magick are just amassed information about the known rules, patterns
and phenomena of different aspects of reality.  The difference between arete and 
the spheres is Arete is understanding and the spheres are knowledge. That is why 
spheres can be studied and discussed easily, but not arete. To be able to use 
(or even learn) the spheres you have to have some understanding of reality 
beforehand, otherwise it is just meaningless information.
     
No Sphere possessed by a mage may be rated higher than his Arete rating, 
so in order to increase your Sphere ratings above one, you must ensure your
Arete is two or higher.  Arete also sets the dice pool for rotes,  So the higher 
it is, the more damage you will do with your attack rotes and the better your 
effects will be.
    
Unlike other traits, Arete can be raised to level ten.
   
Freebie Cost:  6 * Current Level
         
{WWarning:{x {CRaising your Arete to level {W5 {Cwill 'lock' your Avatar rating 
         to its current variable.{x
~
0 quintessence mage_quintessence~

QUINTESSENCE:
One of the most important things in a Mage's life is Quintessence. 
Superficially, it is the raw fuel of Magick. More deeply, Quintessence is the 
very basis of reality. Quantities of Quintessence are the building blocks of 
reality (and potential reality). Quintessence is extremely closely tied with 
Paradox. For every point of Paradox your body is holding, you can hold one less 
of Quintessence.

The most Quintessence you can ever hold is 100.

Also help on:
MAGES, MAGICK, TRADITIONS, SPHERES, ARETE, AVATAR, QUINTESSENCE, ROTES, INTRINSICS
~
-1 PARADOX~

PARADOX:
This is the fear of all Mages. Paradox is simply a fact of reality created by 
the manipulation of the "current" facts of reality, thereby changing reality... 
Where was I? You see my point, paradox is paradox, created by what mages do.

This is the fear of all Mages. Paradox is simply a fact of reality created by 
the facts of reality.

The use of blatant Magick within the constraints of reality can create an 
anomaly within that reality - a Paradox. To prevent this Paradox, mages often 
use Coincidental Magick to fit within the laws of the current reality.

Example of Non-Coincidental Magick (Called Vulgar):
The mage hurls a fireball from his hand at his enemy to incinerate them.

Example of Coincidental Magick:
The mage causes a gas main to 'coincidentally' rupture in the oven behind his 
enemy and then 'coincidentally' discovers a match book in his pocket which he 
lights and throws towards his opponent which 'coincidentally' doesn't go out 
during flight. This alites the foe and incinerates them where they stand 
without altering the rules of the universe... too much.

Be aware though that sometimes things just screw up. A botch can result that 
causes the Mage to gain paradox.. and risk a Paradox Backlash. Which is 
basically reality canceling out the Mage's effect and seeking to prevent future 
ones by eliminating the cause... the Mage.

Every point of Paradox prevents the Mage from storing a point of Quintessence. 
In addition it also increases the chance, and damage of a backlash.

Also help on:
CONVERT, MAGES, MAGICK, TRADITIONS, SPHERES, ARETE, AVATAR, QUINTESSENCE, ROTES
~
0 TASS~

Mages fuel their mystic arts from the energy of creation, quintessence.
While this energy is typically free flowing, and manipulated by skilled
individuals as needed, occasionally concentrations of quintessence bond
together in physical form to be found.  Quintessence in physical form,
permeating an object to its Pattern, is called Tass.  An object of Tass
can have the Quintessence siphoned away and used by the Mage directly.
In addition to using Prime to create Tass by infusing items, certain
items may be found naturally occurring.

The most common form of naturally occurring Tass is found in Faerie
Mushrooms.  These edible mushrooms give a random rush of Quintessence
to a Mage, but have no effect otherwise to someone who is not Awakened.
Faerie Mushrooms spawn randomly, and are found in places of concentrated
power, such as Nodes.

Additionally, any (Magical) item is considered a form of Tass.  Mages who
progress in the sphere of Prime can learn to absorb Quintessence directly
from these magic items.

Also help on:
MAGES, MAGICK, TRADITIONS, SPHERES, ARETE, AVATAR, QUINTESSENCE, ROTES, INTRINSICS
~
-1 MAGICK~

{CMagick{x
      
