0 names naming~

Naming Policy
----------------------------------------------------------------------------
1. This is a White Wolf theme based MUD, therefore names should be based around 
this theme.
 
2. Real words, and therefore compounds word also, are NOT acceptable as 
character names, this includes but isn't limited to MrHappy, Superstud, and
other stupid names of this nature.
 
3. Names taken from popular cartoons, movies, and popular literature are not 
acceptable as player names.
 
4. Names with profane language are not acceptable as player names.
 
5. Names which mimic, insult or otherwise emulate another Immortal or player 
are not acceptable.
 
6. The Immortal Staff, reserves the right to determine wether a name is
acceptable or not, and may act on their own descretion, petitions are to be 
made to the Administration only.
 
7. The Administration reserve the right to make changes to these rules at any
time with or without notification, warning or evidence of sanity.
----------------------------------------------------------------------------
~
0 Get_of_Fenris~

Known as great fighters throughout the land, the Get of Fenris have no qualms 
about showing their ruthlessness.  Believing that mercy is for the weak, they 
demand that quick action be taken against their enemies. Their crusade against 
the wyrm is neverending, and their eagerness to fight on the battlefield never 
fades.  Because of this, they put themselves at odds with the other tribes at 
times.  The Get believe they are superior in battle, and other tribes are irked 
by their arrogance and brashness.  In addition, they have a deep hatred for 
humans as well as the tribes made up primarily of indigenous people, the Uktena 
and Wendigo. They do not fear death, and they have no patience for the weak. 
 
Many of the Get are originally Scandinavian and they migrated with the Vikings 
during their conquests of Europe.  They take great pride in their superior 
bloodline and even today, many of the Get hail from Scandinavian or Germanic 
families. 
 
Also help on: GAROU TRIBES FETISH 
~
0 Silver_Fangs~

The Silver Fangs are the nobility of the Garou.  They are all born into good 
families, and are expected to be treated with respect.  They are good fighters, 
politicians, and most importantly, leaders.  They are often somewhat burdened 
with the task of taking care of many of the other tribes, and act 
condescendingly towards them on occasion.  Unfortunately, as of late, the 
strength and leadership that the Silver Fangs supported the other tribes with 
has been fading.  With new dealings as they are, many of the Silver Fang 
leaders have become overly cautious, or even reclusive. These new ways no 
longer demand respect, but instead make the Silver Fangs appear weak and afraid.
 
Whether it is because of inbreeding, or the corrupting forces of the Wyrm, the 
Silver Fang's noble bloodline is tainted with insanity.  While this taint 
manifests itself in many forms, it is most often a visible weakness. 
 
Also help on: GAROU TRIBES FETISH 
~
0 Black_Furies~

One of the more unique tribes, the Black Furies are composed mainly of female 
Garou.  They are all proud of their heritage, and have been separate from the 
other tribes since prehistoric times.  A strong belief of theirs is that 
Artemis (Luna) wants them to stay away from men.  In respect of her wishes, 
they only allow males of the infertile metis breed into their ranks. 
 
These righteous beings hold steady in their need to protect the Wyld and women 
around the world. They find themselves gravitating towards the few wild areas 
left in the world, and go to great lengths to preserve these places. And 
knowing of the hardships that females go through in male dominated societies, 
they also do their best to protect women of most species. 
 
Their obvious differences make communications between other tribes fairly 
tense. They ally themselves with the Children of Gaia and the Silent Striders.  
And they have a deep hatred for the Get of Fenris and Shadow Lords. The other 
tribes they tend to ignore more than act with or against. 
 
Also help on: GAROU TRIBES FETISH 
~
0 Stargazers~

The members of the Stargazers are the most introspective of any clan.  They 
fear that rusing into things will only cause confusion, and therefore spend 
more time meditating on ideas.  The Stargazers withdrew from werewolf society 
after their pleas to protect the humans went ignored.  Often, they can be seen 
staring into a night's sky, gazing at the stars and moon.  With this, they seem 
to have a special relationship.  They believe the moon to guide and protect 
them in all ways, to keep them safe from the dark nights. 
 
While normally quite peaceful, the Stargazers can be as ferocious as any other 
Garou.  Using the shadows to hide them, they protect the humans from the Wyrm. 
This has brought them a great deal of animosity from other tribes, and made 
them untrustworthy as a whole in their eyes.  Despite this, the Stargazers 
insist that peace must be made in between the tribes, and with the humans, 
before the Wyrm can truly be destroyed. 
 
The Stargazers are known as great wanderers.  They travel through nature, 
bringing no material belongings with them.  During their journeys they often 
breed with outcasts of the human race, others that have fled from the evils of 
society. 
 
Also help on: GAROU TRIBES FETISH 
~
0 assassinate~

{yAssassinate{x
{y       Melee {W*****{x, {yMedicine {W***{x
{W        (Requires Dagger){x

{WSyntax:  {cassassinate {w<target>{x

Truly skilled rogues have mastered the art of surprise, dealing great amounts
of damage against unprepared opponents.  The injury causes by a successful
assassination is grievous indeed, and oftentimes more powerful than a regular
backstab.
 
{WTable Top / Role Play{x
{WSystem:{x  Varied and dependant upon circumstances.

{WOut of Character / Hack and Slash{x
{WSystem:  {xYou must be either sneaking, or your quarry unable to see you.  This
can be accomplished by hiding, or using supernatural powers, or even the target
being asleep and unaware.  With successes on Dexteriy + Stealth (Difficulty 6)
roll, another success on Intelligence + Medicine allows you to pierce the spine.
Failing to pierce the spine will automatically trigger a backstab attempt.

Also help on: ROGUE ASSASSIN BACKSTAB 
~
0 Ground~

Ground is a simple but useful skill that is known by most warriors.  By running 
into their target, they can knock it out of the air, and can stop it from 
flying. This is particularly useful if the opponent is considering fleeing, or 
if a trip attack is in order. 
 
Also help on: TRIP 
~
0 Fortress~

Fortress is one of the many skills a guard has to defend themselves better. By 
using this, a guard may fortify their shield, increasing the armor class on it, 
and therefore making themselves harder to be hit and hurt. While the affects 
last for awhile, it does cost a heavy bit of mana and should be used sparingly. 
 
Also help on: GUARDS 
~
0 Vigor~

{yVigor{x
{y       Athletics {W**{x
 
{WSyntax:  {cvigor{x
 
Many who travel throughout the Dark Ages oftentimes find themselves at
the mercy of long journeys, with limited times for rest.  Many athletic
individuals go through vigorous training, preparing their bodies for the
harsh conditions that lie ahead.  This training allows one to maximize
his or her potential, avoiding wasting precious energy and reserving it
for when it is needed most.  Through this training, one can recall the
proper ways to become more efficient in both speed and endurance.
 
{WTable Top / Role Play{x
{WSystem:  {xHaving trained under exerting conditions, one can make a
Stamina + Athletics Roll (Difficulty based on terrain) to continue
exerting themselves for extended periods of time in their present action.
 
{WOut of Character / Hack and Slash{x
{WSystem:{x  By recalling the vigorous training needed to tone one's body,
you spend a point of Willpower and movement to focus on speed/endurance
training.  With a successful Stamina + Athletics Roll (Difficulty 6),
you speed yourself up for a chance at an additional strike in combat.
Additionally, you gain additional maximum movement for the duration,
based upon your Stamina.  On a critical success, you can increase
your hitroll.
~
