101 Deductions~

{RCURRENTLY OBSOLETE: SEE BELOW{x

Looking at the damage list, it may seem that the numbers are a bit high. To 
equal this out, weapons are reduced in their level of damage if they get extra 
affects. 
 
Poison, Vorpal, Shocking flags: Deduct 5 levels. 
Slow or Shocking flags:         Deduct 8 levels. 
Frost flag:                     Deduct 12 levels. 
Flaming and Vampiric Flags:     Deduct 15 levels. 
Anti-evil, good, or neutral:    Add 3 levels. 
For every 10 hp, mp, or mv:     Deduct 1 level. 
For every -save or attribute:   Deduct 1 level. 
Two-handed weapon:              Add 10 levels. 
Every pair of hr/dr:            Deduct 1 level. 
 
No other flags or affects should be added to weapons unless they are approved 
by a high ranking immortal. 

{YNOTE:  The only flag allowed currently is the Two-hand flag.  Use proper 
addition to level.{x
 
Also help on: DAMAGE_CHART 
~
-1 CHARACTER~

CHARACTER :
Who are you?  Where did you come from?  Are your parents still alive? All of 
these questions and many more are ones that you should think on when creating a 
character on Haven of the Embraced.

In order to get anywhere on Haven, you MUST roleplay.  To help you along with 
this, we have created a Character Sheet.  It lists all the different 
information which drives your character ICly and OOCly.  To see this sheet, 
please type CS, CS2 or CS3 while in gameplay.

Also help on CREATE CHARACTER_SHEET
~
-1 CREATE~

CREATE :
The command 'Create' allows a player to begin placing their stats into their 
character sheet.  There is a set of directions within each stage of creation 
that will walk you through the process. Create is meant to allow older players 
access to new attributes and abilities. Don't be worried if Create tells you 
that there is nothing new to update.

Also help on: CHARACTER CHARACTER_SHEET
~
