~
0 bloodpool bp bloodpoint~

Vampires and Ghouls fuel themselves through the intake and use of blood.  The
maximum amount of blood that a Vampire or Ghoul is able to store in her body
to turn into usable Vitae is referred to as her Bloodpool (BP).  There are
many ways to spend and replenish this supply throughout your time on Haven.

A Vampire's maximum Bloodpool is dependant upon her {yGeneration{x:
Generation 13 ... 10 Bloodpool MAX  Generation  8 ... 12 Bloodpool MAX
Generation 12 ... 10 Bloodpool MAX  Generation  7 ... 13 Bloodpool MAX
Generation 11 ... 10 Bloodpool MAX  Generation  6 ... 14 Bloodpool MAX
Generation 10 ... 10 Bloodpool MAX  Generation  5 ... 15 Bloodpool MAX
Generation  9 ... 11 Bloodpool MAX  Generation  4 ... 16 Bloodpool MAX

If a Vampire's current Bloodpool drops below 1, she enters into a frenzy
and begins losing health points.  If you do not regain blood soon, you run
the risk of falling into Torpor.  Vampires typically regain blood by feeding
in combat, or on corpses, but may also be nourished by other players.

A Ghoul has a maximum of 10 Bloodpool.  While a ghoul does not frenzy upon
reaching low blood, she does risk dying if all of the blood is removed from
her system.  Ghouls can only regain blood from a vampiric source, therefore
the two most common ways to regain vitae are from beheading torped vampires
and being nourished by vampire players.

{RAlso help on: {WVampire Ghoul Torpor Nourish Generation Feed{x
~
0 generations_ic~

GENERATION :
Generation refers, just as in mortal society to your place in your family 
tree, but in a Vampire's case, how far removed from Caine they are.  Caine was 
the First.  His Children, the Second generation in White Wolf's World of 
Darkness are said to be powerful like a demigod, should they still even exist. 
The Third generation, the Antediluvians, meaning Before the Flood. are also 
quite powerful and they are greatly feared by those who still walk the night. 
Neither of these two generations walk the world of Haven.

The Fourth generation, The Methuselahs are the powerful Vampires that still
walk the streets.  They have lived many, many centuries, and have removed
themselves from the petty squabblings of the younger generations for the peace 
and tranquility of their own unlives.  They are so powerful that the thought of 
embracing one to be so close to them in power, keeps them from attempting such 
a thing.

The Fifth, Sixth, Seventh and Eight generations are usually referd to as 
elders, as they have lived for many years and are able to perform many
different tasks without worry. They are able to embrace and bring new
Childer into their clan. They are responsible for teaching the neonates,
(newly embraced) what it is to be a Vampire, and a member of their clan.

The Ninth and Tenth Generations, while no longer neonates, are barely elders. 
While they may hold position of authoirty within a clan, they do not have the 
physical power or mental capacity that their elders do, and are often reminded 
of this, sometimes through very harsh means.

Those of the Eleventh, Twelfth and Thirteenth generation are the neonates. The 
thin-blooded. They have very few abilities and although they are no longer 
mortal, they are nowhere near as powerful as those of what are considered the 
higher generations.  These Childer must scrounge for what little respect they 
get, whether it be through a boon from an older Vampire, or simply falling upon 
a little bit of information that they can use to topple another Vampire.  Like 
the Methuselahs, those of the Thirteenth generation can not embrace.  Their 
blood is not strong enough to pass on the abilities of the Kindred.

Also help on: VAMPIRE TORPOR NOURISH DISCIPLINE REGENERATION BLOODPOOL
DPOINT
~
0 character_sheet charsheet cs cs1 cs2 cs3~

Characters in a roleplaying game are defined in multiple aspects. The player imparts a
personality to the character, but most are defined by a series of traits. In the 
Storytelling System these include Attributes, Abilities, and a number of Advantages 
including Health Levels, Willpower, Backgrounds, among others.
{x
While not a complete picture of who a character is, these traits provide a means for 
describing a character's basic information. It lets you know, at a glance, who this 
character is and a basic idea of what they know. The details of how a character developed 
these traits and what the specifics are is left to be roleplayed by the player.
{x
Some traits are combined with others to form a Dicepool in order to perform actions. 
Occasionally, traits are rolled by themselves and in the case of traits such as Willpower, 
are only ever rolled by themselves. In any case, success or failure at a task is 
determined by a combination of the traits a character possesses, and their luck on a 
diceroll.
{x
Character sheets on Haven are formed in one of two ways. During the initial character 
creation, players are given the option of taking one of three stock Character Archetypes. 
These give an easy way to populate the sheet with stats without having to place each point 
individually. Players can also choose to forgo the Archetypes and craft a custom character 
sheet once they've entered the game.
{x
After creation, traits can be increased by the expenditure of Freebies. Each type of 
trait has its own cost associated with increasing the rating, usually a multiple of the
Current Rating. Typing the '{cfreebie{x' command will give a list of all the types of 
traits the character can increase and their costs.
{x
Syntax:
{ccreate{w - Initiate the Creation process to set traits.{x
{ccharsheet {w({ccs{w) - Basic Information, Attributes and Abilities.{x
{ccharsheet2 {w({ccs2{w) - Advantages such as Backgrounds, Willpower and race-specific traits.{x
{ccharsheet3 {w({ccs3{w) - Secondary Abilities and sub-skills of other abilities.{x
~
-1 ATTRIBUTES~

ATTRIBUTES :
Attributes refers to the Physical, Social and Mental statistics of the players 
on Haven.  When choosing your attributes, think of what type of things your 
character is good at doing.  If you excel at figuring out puzzles, then the 
mental section is going to be your primary section. If you are a brawler, then 
physical attributes would be your primary section.  Finally, if your character 
is the social butterfly that tries to use their looks and charm to get by, then 
the social section is what you will want to select as your primary section.  
Secondary and tertiary attributes are assigned the same way as the primary ones 
are.  All players begin with one dot in each of their sections. The available
attributes from the character sheet are:

Also help on:  PHYSICAL STRENGTH DEXTERITY STAMINA SOCIAL CHARISMA
MANIPULATION APPEARANCE MENTAL PERCEPTION INTELLIGENCE WITS
~
-1 stamina~

Stamina
 
Stamina measures general health and resistance to pain; it indicates how long 
you can exert yourself and how much physical punishment you can sustain. 
Stamina is your staying power, both physically and mentally, and one of its 
most important elements is the will to live.
 
Specialties: Catlike Reflexes, Swift, Sure-Footed, Light Touch
 
*Poor:  Your existence is a constant parade of minor (and major) miseries. In 
life, you got hurt easily and healed slowly.
**Average: You're of average health.
***Good:  In life, you seldom succumbed to the illnesses sweeping around you.
In unlife, you resist injury better than many vampires.
****Exceptional:  You keep going in the face of challenges that exhaust others.
*****Outstanding:  You have the constant grace of a demigod.
 
See also:  Strength, Dexterity
~
-1 charisma~

Charisma
 
Charisma measures your aptitude for enticing and fascinating others. You use 
Charisma to win others over to you emotionally and get them to trust you. This 
Trait reflects a charismatic personality more than it does an overt 
manipulation of others. It is a sum of your presence, charm and power of 
influence. Charisma reflects your power to convince others to put faith in you.
 
Specialties: Charming, Eloquent, Outgoing, Captivating, Commanding, 
Inspiring
 
*Poor: Others avoid being around you.
**Average: You are likable.
***Good: People trust and confide in you.
****Exceptional: Something draws people to you.
*****Outstanding: You could lead a nation.
 
See also:  Manipulation, Appearance
~
-1 perception~

Perception
 
This Trait indicates your awareness of the environment around you. While 
Perception is sometimes used consciously, such as when you search for 
something, it more often works intuitively - you simply notice something. At 
base, Perception is a sensitivity to the world, an open-eyed quality common 
among children (for whom the world is a boundless and mysterious place), and 
seldom present among the most jaded.
 
Perception is used to see if you have the insight to understand or realize a 
certain fact or concept. It can help indicate your degree of alertness to 
ambushes, the subtext of a noble's speech or the subtleties of color in a 
painting.
 
Specialties: Insightful, Attentive, Paranoid, Keen-Eyed
 
*Poor: You are blind to anything but the obvious.
**Average: You are unaware of the subtle interactions that occur around you.
***Good: You are aware of moods and textures.
****Exceptional: You are constantly alert to the nuances of life.
*****Outstanding: You can see a needle in a haystack.
 
See also:  Intelligence, Wits
~
-1 ABILITIES~

ABILITIES :
Abilities are all the Talents, Skills and Knowledges thet a person learns
throughout his life whether it be through formal schooling, job training, or 
just sheer natural ability.  It is from these abilities that one is able to 
perform in certain situations.

Also help on: TALENTS SKILLS KNOWLEDGES
~
-1 TALENTS~

TALENTS :
Talents are those things that come naturally to someone.  They are not "gifts
from the gods".  They are things that can not be taught.  They are inate
abilities that simply become more natural and practiced over time.  Available
talents are : Acting, Alertness, Athletics, Brawl, Dodge, Empathy,
Intimidation, Leadership, Streetwise amd Subterfuge.

For further help on Talents, type "help (specific Talent)".

Also help on: ABILITIES SKILLS KNOWLEDGES
~
-1 ALERTNESS~

Alertness
 
Over the years, you have become practiced in noticing all that happens around 
you, even if you are not actively concentrating upon the surroundings. This 
Talent dictates not the ability to search a specific area, but rather the 
ability to stay alert for a long period of time. Alertness simply indicates how 
aware you are of the world around you. It describes how much attention you pay 
to things other than the rumbling of your belly or the doubts in your mind.
 
*{WNovice{x: You tend to be alert to changes, moreso than most.
**{WPracticed{x: You are watchful and very attentive to your surroundings.
***{WCompetent{x: You are highly vigilant.
****{WExpert{x: You are a truly cautious individual and rarely let down your 
guard.
*****{WMaster{x: You notice everything that goes on around you.
 
Possessed by: Sentries, Hunters, Burglars, Messengers, Vagabonds
{WSpecialties{x: Traps, Ambushes, Forests, Crowds, Noises, Paranoia
~
-1 ATHLETICS~

Athletics
 
This Ability describes your general athletic prowess and skill at physical 
games. It determines your ability to jump across a chasm, swim through a storm, 
throw a rock, vault a fence or climb a tree. Athletics concerns complex motor 
actions; physical actions requiring only one type of motor action, such as 
lifting, do not use the Athletics score, nor do athletic actions classified 
under another Ability. (Wrestling, for instance, would fall under Brawl.)
 
*{WNovice{x: Serf
**{WPracticed{x: Squire
***{WCompetent{x: Trained knight
****{WExpert{x: Skilled juggler or tumbler
*****{WMaster{x: Paragon among mortals Olympian at any event.
 
Possessed by: Entertainers, Squires, Barbarians, Youths, Elite Warriors
{WSpecialties{x: Swimming, Juggling, Tumbling, Dancing, Thrown Objects
~
-1 BRAWL~

Brawl
 
You know how to fight unarmed, as well as with casual weapons such as pokers 
and table legs. This Ability includes such maneuvers as punching, kicking, 
grappling, throttling, throwing, gouging and biting. Brawling can get quite 
ruthless, but generally it is a nonlethal form of combat.
 
*Novice: You know what to do, but you haven't had much experience. 
**Practiced: You know where to hit people and make it hurt.
***Competent: Nobody in your village bothers you anymore
****Expert: You can take a sword away from a robber with little trouble.
*****Master: You can wrestle bears to the ground.
 
Possessed by: Soldiers, Bullies, Brigands, Rustics 
Specialties: Armlocks, Boxing, Wrestling, Grappling, Throws, Showing Off
~
0 falsecomfort false_comfort~

{GFalse Comfort{x
{G        Homid {W(Rank 5) {xor {GWarder {W(Rank 5){x
 
Humanity has done much to surround itself with comfort and safety.
People have developed armor to protect themselves from their own
weapons, locks to keep out their own brothers and walls to shelter them
from the beasts at their doors.  But the ancestor-spirits remember when
these comforts were but dreams in the minds of clever humans, and they
can teach the Garou how to bypass them.  A Garou using this Gift does
not shred armor or smash through doors, he simply ignores them entirely.
 
{WTable Top / Role Play{x
{WSystem:  {xSpend one Gnosis point and roll Gnosis (diff 7).  For one
turn per success, the Garou is completely unaffected by human technology
unless he chooses to be.  The character can see, walk, or reach through
anything crafted by humanity including walls, armor and other clothing.
 
{WOut of Character / Hack and Slash{x
{WSyntax:  {cbeseech 'false comfort'{x
While active, this Gift allows you to pass through doors.  Additionally,
your autoattacks ignore enemy armor ratings.  This Gift costs a point
of Gnosis to activate.
~
0 empathy_talent~

Empathy
 
You understand and can sympathize with the emotions of others, and are thus 
able to respond to them appropriately. You can often discern the motives behind 
someone's actions by simply listening to him. You can also detect when you are 
being told lies. Empathy has a down side, however - because you are so open to 
the feelings of others you often feel the same emotions as those around you.
 
*{WNovice{x: Gossipy widows feel they can trust you.
**{WPracticed{x: Occasionally you get sympathetic pains from others.
***{WCompetent{x: You have an amazing insight into others' motivations.
****{WExpert{x: No lies ever get past your scrutiny.
*****{WMaster{x: You often finish other people's sentences.
 
Possessed by: Gossips, Skilled Merchants, Priests, Parents, Fortunetellers
{WSpecialties{x: Emotions, Truths, Family Problems, Personalities, 
Background Emotion
~
-1 INTIMIDATION~

Intimidation
 
The art of intimidation comes in many forms, ranging from a subtle suggestion 
to outright physical damage. Each method of intimidation has its time and 
place. You understand the science of being overbearing and know how to use it 
to get what you want. People with high Intimidation scores seem to radiate an 
aura of authority.
 
*{WNovice{x: Stray dogs cross the street to avoid you.
**{WPracticed{x: You win an occasional staredown.
***{WCompetent{x: Your gaze is very unsettling.
****{WExpert{x: You can dominate foreigners on their home ground.
*****{WMaster{x: You can make vicious animals turn tail and run.
 
Possessed by: Brigands, Witch-Hunters, Sovereigns, Torturers, Knights
{WSpecialties{x: Staredowns, Subtle Hints, Overt Violence, Threats, Political
~
-1 LEADERSHIP~

Leadership
 
You can get people to follow your lead and obey your orders through exerting 
authority and by example. Leadership isn't so much knowing the techniques of 
getting people to follow you as it is being the type of person people will 
follow. Leadership is often used in conjunction with Charisma.
 
*{WNovice{x: You could organize a work party.
**{WPracticed{x: Your voice is a dominant one, and you can demand silence.
***{WCompetent{x: You can rally your neighbors when the need arises.
****{WExpert{x: You attract followers without really trying.
*****{WMaster{x: You could be the next Charlemagne.
 
Possessed by: Nobles, Military Officers, Constabulary, Churchmen
{WSpecialties{x: Commands, Orate, Compelling, Friendly, Noble, Military
 
OOC:  Your leadership rating on Haven directly affects how many followers you 
may have in your group. Every person can handle 2 followers, each dot of
Leadership adds 2 potential group members.
~
-1 streetwise larceny legerdemain~

Legerdemain (Formerly Streetwise)
 
This Talent actually covers a wide range of criminal activities, including both 
knowledge of the physical aspect of skills and the ability to find and deal 
with criminal groups. That said, there isn't much of an organized underworld in 
medieval Europe. Most criminals act alone or with small bands of friends. 
Cities are simply too small and communications too poor to support large 
criminal syndicates. Only in the largest cities - Venice, Genoa, Paris, London
 - might large groups be found.
 
However, this Talent is still very useful, both for dealing with these 
scattered groups and for committing petty crimes. First and foremost, 
Legerdemain allows you to blend in with the local scene without drawing 
attention to yourself. Gossip, felony theft and street slang are also impacted 
by using this Talent. Finally, those skilled at Legerdemain can perform minor 
criminal acts involving sleight of hand (drugging drinks or cutting purses, for 
instance).
 
For example, the locks of the Middle Ages may be picked with Dexterity + 
Legerdemain (usually difficulty 8); moving a wax seal from one document to 
another requires an Intelligence + Legerdemain roll (difficulty 8).
 
*{WNovice{x: You can get through a simple latched door.
**{WPracticed{x: You can spot a careless cutpurse.
***{WCompetent{x: You could make a living at theft.
****{WExpert{x: You make an excellent burglar, forger and spy.
*****{WMaster{x: You could steal a kingdom's crown jewels.
 
Possessed by: Robbers, Beggars, Vagabonds, Traveling Players
{WSpecialties{x: Picking Pockets, Rumor Mill, Fencing, Slang Terms, Lockpicking
~
-1 SUBTERFUGE~

Subterfuge
 
You know how to conceal your own motives; moreover, you know how to decipher 
the motives of others and how to use those against them. The secrets and 
intrigues of others interest you, and you work at understanding their 
weaknesses. A command of this skill makes you the ultimate conversationalist, 
or the ultimate spy.
 
*{WNovice{x: You understand tact.
**{WPracticed{x: You could hold out on the tax collector.
***{WCompetent{x: You could woo two women at once.
****{WExpert{x: You could sell pig sweat as alkahest.
*****{WMaster{x: You could, with time, convince your archenemy to trust you.
 
Possessed by: Courtiers, Charlatans, Wooers, Minstrels, Traveling Players, Spies
{WSpecialties{x: Finding Weaknesses, Seduction, Selective Omission, Fast-Talk, 
Flattery, Changing the Subject
~
-1 SKILLS~

SKILLS :
Skills are things which one can be trained in, and takes practice in order to 
master the ability.  Many of them are seen as 'god given gifts' and for many 
people some of these skills come very quickly.  Available Skills are: Animal 
Ken, Archery, Crafts, Etiquitte, Melee, Music, Riding, Security, Stealth, and 
Survival.

For further help on Skills, type "help (specific Skill)".

Also help on: ABILITIES TALENTS KNOWLEDGES
~
-1 animal ken animalken animal_ken~

Animal Ken
 
Animals do not behave in the same way that humans do under the same 
circumstances. The ability to understand the actions of animals can come in 
quite handy. Those characters skilled in Animal Ken can not only predict the 
actions of animals, but can use this knowledge to calm or enrage them. Animal 
Ken also is the Skill used to train animals. It is worth noting that many- 
animals are uneasy around vampires, and Animal Ken is invaluable for any 
Cainite planning to ride horses.
 
* {WNovice{x: You can befriend a domesticated animal.
**{WPracticed{x: You can teach a dog to come when you call.
***{WCompetent{x: You could train a hunting hound.
****{WExpert{x: You could be the king's own falconer.
*****{WMaster{x: You could domesticate a wild animal.
 
Possessed by: Kennel Masters, Falconers, Stablehands, Manor Lords, Squires, 
Hermits
{WSpecialties{x: Dogs, Raptors, Horses, Bears, Farm Animals
~
-1 ARCHERY~

Archery
 
You can fire bows and crossbows. You can also string a bow, and care for and 
make minor repairs to bows, crossbows, arrows and quarrels.
 
*{WNovice{x: Your father showed you how.
**{WPracticed{x: You practiced regularly on the village green.
***{WCompetent{x: You could find work as a forester.
****{WExpert{x: You could make extra money at the archery competitions at local 
fairs and tournaments.
*****{WMaster{x: Robin Hood or William Tell.
 
Possessed By: Foresters, Poachers, Competitors, Militias, Bandits
{WSpecialties{x: Target, Forests, Hunting, Moving Target, Quick Shot
~
-1 CRAFTS~

Crafts
 
Craft Skills are simply the professional skills most medieval people have, 
which they use to survive. Remember that almost everyone at this time works 
with their hands. Some may have two Crafts (e.g., a farmer who also works as a 
carpenter), but most specialize in one.
 
Such Skills often include various petty abilities. So, Farming does not just 
cover sowing and reaping; it includes handling sheep and domestic animals, 
repairing buildings and driving carts. Goldsmithing allows a character to 
evaluate gems and metals, to speculate upon the age of jewelry, etc.
 
Examples of Craft Skills include Farming (the most common), Carpentry, 
Blacksmithing, Glazing, Stonemasonry, Wheelwright, Tanner, Brewing, 
Goldsmithing, Dyeing, etc.
 
*{WNovice{x: An apprentice or part-time worker.
**{WPracticed{x:  A newly qualified craftsman or inexpert farmer.
***{WCompetent{x: An experienced, competent professional, earning a fair living.
****{WExpert{x: A respected master craftsman.
****{WMaster{x: An artisan who has elevated his trade to the level of an art, 
or a farmer who could make crops grow through a drought.
 
Possessed By: Artisans, Farmers, Townsfolk
{WSpecialties{x: Detail, Working Quickly, Inventive, Organization, Evaluate
{WExpertise{x:  Architecture, Armory, Blacksmithing, Boat-Building, Jewelry, 
Masonry, Sewing & Embroidery, Woodworking, Etc.
~
-1 ETIQUETTE~

Etiquette
 
You understand the small nuances of social life and are able to conduct 
yourself in a manner that is both unobtrusive and gracious. You understand how 
to get along well with mortal society, whether courtly or rustic. Your 
specialty is the culture with which you are most familiar. You use Etiquette 
during actions such as dancing, seduction and haggling. Etiquette is also used 
when engaging in diplomacy.
 
*{WNovice{x: You know when to shut up.
**{WPracticed{x: You know how to address a local lord or alderman.
***{WCompetent{x: You understand the nuances of courtly manners.
****{WExpert{x: You could get along with just about anybody.
*****{WMaster{x: You can seat blood enemies at the same table and keep them 
happy.
 
Possessed by: Envoys, Nobles, Heralds, Courtiers, Handmaidens
{WSpecialties{x: Courtly Manners, Street Culture, Peasants, Foreign Customs
~
-1 MELEE~

Melee
 
In the Dark Medieval world, skill in armed combat can be vital to a vampire's 
survival. Proficiency in this Skill allows you to use hand-held weapons. Melee 
covers everything from simple knives, axes and swords to wooden stakes and 
20-foot pikes. Although not every Cainite will have possessed this Ability in 
life (lords are often loath to teach their vassals to fight), many learn it 
from their sires or other sources afterward.
 
*{WNovice{x: You've seen a knife being used.
**{WPracticed{x: Peasant militia
***{WCompetent{x: Typical knight
****{WExpert{x: Any weapon is deadly in your grasp.
*****{WMaster{x: Lancelot
 
Possessed by: Soldiers, Militia, Robbers, Lords, Barbarians 
{WSpecialties{x: Swords, Axes, Knives, Clubs, Disarms
~
0 music jukebox~

Within Haven, there are certain entities that can play songs for a room. 
When you come across one of these 'jukeboxes', you can spend gold to play a
song.  
 
{WSyntax:  {cplay{x
~
-1 commerce security~

Commerce (Formerly Security)
 
Commerce is the ability to successfully bring goods to market, with all that 
entails.  It includes the ability to evaluate goods and to identify who would 
want them, knowledge of trade routes and fairs and skill at negotiation prices. 
Commerce is a catch-all ability, and you should choose one class of goods as a 
field of expertise when you first purchase it.  You can use commerce outside 
your field of expertise to identify potential markets and experts in the field 
and to negotiate and haggle over just about anything. Evaluating an item or a 
trade route with which you have no experience is beyond you, and it counts as 
acting without the required ability.
 
In the dark medieval, the line between legitimate and illegitimate trade is 
blurry to non-existent, and commerce comes into play just as much when buying 
cheese as when hiring a mercenary, soliciting a prostitute or selling stolen 
goods.  As such, commerce conveys a general sense of the shadier side of life 
- what modern folk might call being streetwise.
 
*{WNovice{x-You can get a fair price when you bring the harvest to market.
**{WPracticed{x-You can broker exchanges in your field of expertise and know 
who in the vicinity deals in what trades, legitimate or otherwise.
***{WCompetent{x-You can make a good living as a merchant or moneylender. You 
can draw on the expertise of those in other trades without difficulty.
****{WExpert{x-You are one of the preeminent experts in your field, and you are 
rarely (if ever) taken advantage of.  No market is closed for you.
*****{WMaster{x-You are a master merchant, expert in commerce spanning the 
continent.
 
Possessed by: Artisans, Farmers, Mercenaries, Ne'er-do-wells, Prostitutes, 
Traders
{WSpecialties{x: Evaluation, Negotiation, Swindling, Trade Routes
{WExpertise{x: Clothing, Foodstuffs, Livestock, Mercenaries, Relics, Silks, 
Slaves, Spices, Stolen Goods, Wine, etc
~
-1 SECURITY~

SECURITY :
This is not currently coded.  Once it is there will be a list of skills which 
it applies to.

Also help on: ABILITIES TALENTS SKILLS KNOWLEDGES
~
-1 STEALTH~

Stealth
 
Stealth is the ability to sneak about or hide without being seen or heard, and 
is often rolled against another character's Perception. Stealth is of extreme 
importance when vampires engage in the Hunt.
 
*{WNovice{x: You can hide in the dark.
**{WPracticed{x: You can hide in the shadows.
***{WCompetent{x: You are an accomplished hunter.
****{WExpert{x: You could walk silently over two inches of dry leaves.
*****{WMaster{x: You could sneak up on a pack of wolves.
 
Possessed by: Burglars, Spies, Scouts, Hunters, Vampires 
{WSpecialties{x: Prowl, Hide, Lurk, Shadows, Crowds, Crawling, Wilderness
~
-1 SURVIVAL~

Survival
 
The wilderness is a dangerous place, at least for those who do not understand 
it. The skill of Survival includes seeking shelter, finding a direct route 
through and relative safety in the wilderness, and tracking. When you use 
Stealth in the wilderness, you cannot roll more dice for your Stealth rating 
then you have in Survival.
 
*{WNovice{x: You can survive a five-mile trek.
**{WPracticed{x: You are familiar with the wilderness.
***{WCompetent{x: You can feed yourself adequately for long periods of time.
****{WExpert{x: You are at home in the wild. 
*****{WMaster{x: You could live off the land for years on end.
 
Possessed by: Barbarians, Hunters, Bandits, Refugees, Hermits 
{WSpecialties{x: Tracking, Highlands, Edible Plants, Marsh, Hunting
~
-1 knowledges~

KNOWLEDGES :
Knowedges are those abilities which are considered to have been learned through 
some sort of formal training.  While someone might have a natural ability and 
do well in one of these areas, without the formal training behind them, they 
are just another 'Jack-of-all-trades'.

Knowledges are:  Academics, Finance, Investigation, Law, Linguistics, Medicine,
Occult, Politics, Science and Theology.

For further help on Knowledges, type "help (specific Knowledge)".

Also help on: ABILITIES TALENTS SKILLS
~
-1 ACADEMICS~

Academics
 
You understand Latin, can read and write, and have been taught something of 
theology and philosophy. This is the standard medieval education, and requires 
that you have attended at least a cathedral school or monastery. A high rating 
indicates that you attended one of the universities, in Paris, Salerno, Oxford 
or Bologna. This education did not come cheap. You, your parents or your 
guardians obviously had some wealth.
 
Remember, most medieval people are entirely illiterate and women especially are 
not allowed the same education as the men, if any at all. Without some 
understanding of Academics you can neither read nor write.
 
*{WDabbler{x: You can speak Latin, read and (kind of) write. You've heard of 
Aristotle.
**{WStudent{x: Your Latin grammar is excellent, and you have a good grounding 
in math, philosophy and theology.
***{WLearned{x: You are well versed in the writings of learned theologians and 
pagan philosophers like Aristotle.
****{WScholar{x: You are qualified to teach in any university and can debate 
with the finest minds in Europe.
*****{WSavant{x: You are a learned theologian and could teach a thing or two to 
Aristotle.
 
Possessed by: Ranking Priests, Monks, Teachers, Scribes, Royal Administrators
{WSpecialties{x: Theology, Mathematics, Calligraphy, Metaphysics, Heresy, 
Grammar
{WExpertise{x: Trivium, Quadrivium
~
-1 finance seneschal~

Seneschal (Formerly Finance)
 
During your breathing days (or perhaps in your unlife), you were responsible 
for managing and maintaining a household or organization. Maybe you were Mother 
Superior or the abbot of a convent or monastery, or you might have been the 
chief steward of a nobleman. Perhaps you maintained a cathedral, or you were 
simply the lady of the house. This reflects your knowledge and experience in 
balancing the books, keeping inventory of the larder and wine cellar, managing 
the servants, entertaining guests, keeping the house and lands in good repair, 
and in general making certain that the household, abbey, cathedral, guildhouse 
or whatever was in good running order. Even a farmer might have some similar 
ability in making sure there was enough money for rent and keeping his farm in 
order.
 
Along with the attendant experience, this Knowledge may allow you to evaluate 
how another household is running (and to spot and correct problems), appraise 
quality of trade goods or entertain a guest even if you're not in your usual 
household.
 
*{WDabbler{x: You can keep a smaller place running without too many problems, 
and know how much money is available.
**{WStudent{x: You can balance your books and budget for expenses, and guests 
are never a problem.
***{WLearned{x: You can handle a larger house hold with no one assisting you, 
and your guests always have a good night.
****{WScholar{x: You can manage a large household or series of smaller 
households with no trouble.
*****{WSavant{x: You can keep your house running even during the most difficult 
times, and your superiors consider you indispensible.
 
Possessed by: Innkeepers, Noblewomen, Wives, Chief Stewards, Seneschals
{WSpecialties{x: Kitchens, Hostels, Noble Households, Accounting, Innkeeping, 
Taverns, Religious Orders
~
-1 INVESTIGATION~

Investigation
 
You are trained to notice all sorts of details others might miss, and at high 
levels may function as a detective. This Knowledge also reflects a character's 
ability to do research, both in libraries (rare) and through questioning.
 
*{WDabbler{x: You'd notice the footprints on the stable floor.
**{WStudent{x: You can get information by buying a few drinks.
***{WLearned{x: You can tell an accidental fire from a deliberate one.
****{WScholar{x: You catch minutiae with a brief scan of the room.
*****{WSavant{x: Brother Cadfael
 
Possessed by: Spies, Constables, Tax Collectors, Abbots, Bounty Hunters
{WSpecialties{x: Search, Prowl, Locate Informant, Monastery Records, Shadowing
~
-1 LAW~

Law
 
Prisons do not exist as a formal institution, and a criminal's rights are often 
whatever the local authorities feel like granting. This Knowledge allows 
characters to know what is locally illegal and how severely infractions are 
punished. More often, this Knowledge allows local judges, officials and rulers 
to settle disputes over property and the like. In a feudal society, the laws of 
ownership are of paramount importance.
 
*{WDabbler{x: Practical knowledge; city guard
**{WStudent{x: Captain of the guard
***{WLearned{x: Town official
****{WScholar{x: Experienced judge
*****{WSavant{x: King Solomon
 
Possessed by: Constabulary, Judges, Criminals, Sovereigns 
{WSpecialties{x: Courts, Local Law, Punishments, Criminal, Laws of Ownership, 
Nobles' Rights
~
-1 LINGUISTICS~

Linguistics
 
It is assumed that you can speak your natural language, but you must purchase 
any other languages you wish your character to speak. For each level of 
Linguistics, your character may fluently speak another language. However, 
Linguistics also gives a character an understanding of the structure of 
language, which is in turn the basis of thought. With this Ability, you can 
identify accents. You also have a chance of figuring out phrases from languages 
related to the languages you know. For instance, you might be able to decipher 
some vulgar French (a Romance language) if you know Latin. NOTE: You do not 
need to purchase this to speak Latin if you have Academics.
 
*{WDabbler{x: One additional language.
**{WStudent{x: Two additional languages.
***{WLearned{x: Three additional languages.
****{WScholar{x: Four additional languages.
*****{WSavant{x: Five additional languages
 
Possessed by: Travelers, Scholars, Diplomats, Interpreters
{WSpecialties{x: Curse Words, Technical, Diplomatic, Political
~
-1 MEDICINE~

Medicine
 
Medieval medicine is very primitive by modern standards. Even the simplest 
internal surgery has a difficulty factor of 9. In practical terms, this 
Knowledge is only useful for basic "first aid"- stopping bleeding, treating 
burns - and for simple procedures like treating fractures, fevers or stopping 
wounds from festering.
 
*{WDabbler{x: You know a little about binding wounds.
**{WStudent{x: You can bleed someone with little risk.
***{WLearned{x: You can diagnose and treat simple illnesses.
****{WScholar{x: You can deliver a child and rarely lose the mother.
*****{WSavant{x: You could advance medicine to the next level in your area of 
expertise.
 
Possessed by: Apothecaries, Midwives, Barbers, Field Surgeons
{WSpecialties{x: Herbs, Poison Treatment, Battle Wounds, Disease, Leeching, 
Childbirth, Petty Surgery, First Aid, Diagnosis
 
{WOOC{x: Use of the Bandage skill is given by the Medicine Knowledge
~
-1 OCCULT~

Occult
 
This Knowledge is a catch-all dealing with local folklore, arcane texts, 
ancient legends and most other forms of supernatural facts and hearsay. This 
understanding of the more sinister side of the world includes knowledge of 
curses, rituals, magic and mysticism, and contains much that is only 
speculation and fantasy. This Knowledge is of the utmost interest to many 
vampires, and pursuit of this Knowledge may indeed become a major facet of your 
chronicle. A 4 or 5 rating indicates a deep understanding of vampires and other 
aspects of the occult (mostly what is patently false).
 
*{WDabbler{x: You've heard some tales.
**{WStudent{x: You listen to the local wise woman's rambling.
***{WLearned{x: You've found proof to back up some of your beliefs.
****{WScholar{x: You have found great secrets hidden among the dross.
*****{WSavant{x: Fully initiated in many of the great mysteries. You don't need 
your sire to tell you what's going on!
 
Possessed by: Heretical Scholars, Vampires, Pagans, Hedge Wizards, Kabbalists
{WSpecialties{x: Vampires, Witches, Mystical Powers, Cults, Ancient Wisdom, The 
Kabbala
 
~
-1 POLITICS~

Politics
 
This Knowledge provides a familiarity with the politics of the day, including 
the people in charge and how they got there. It can be applied to almost any 
organization, from the Church to a local goal. This can be an essential Ability 
when attempting to deal with mortal authorities in any way. This Ability even 
has some influence on being a capable politician yourself. Long familiarity 
with a subject can sometimes give one ideas....
 
*Dabbler: Casual observer
**Student: Local herald
***Learned: Aspiring heir
****Scholar: Courtier
*****Savant: Eminence grilse
 
Possessed by: Lords, Courtiers, Heralds, Jesters 
Specialties: Feudalism, City, Religious, Heraldry, Vampiric Hierarchies
~
-1 performance~

Performance is the ability to perform artistic feats.  It covers both the 
technical aspects of the chosen form of expression and the social knowledge of 
what audiences like.  Performance is useful outside your field of expertise to 
evaluate another's skill.
 
*{WNovice{x-You can entertain friends and family when more skillful 
alternatives aren't available
**{WPracticed{x-You take part in local entertainments on a regular basis, and 
you do fairly well at them.
***{WCompetent{x-You can make a living as an entertainer, and you enjoy a 
reputation as a good one to call upon.
****{WExpert{x-Your fellow performers study your work carefully.  The masses 
flock to see you In your specialty.
*****{WMaster{x-You can pick and choose your audiences and you are always in 
demand almost everywhere you go.
 
Possessed By:  Musicians, Troubadours, Actors, Ladies, Spinsters, Monks and Nuns
