1 potence~

{RPotence{x
{R       Potence {W*{x
 
This Discipline defines the superior strength that vampires possess. This 
additional physical might allows great feats to be accomplished, far beyond 
what a normal mortal would be able to perform. Potence allows vampires to jump 
and leap greater distances, lift greater weights, and inflict greater harm upon 
objects and individuals when they are punched or hit.

{WTable Top / Role Play{x
System: The characters rating in Potence provides her with 150% more strength 
with each level attained. This means that you can do 1 more health level of 
damage each turn than normal with each level. So if you have level 1 Potence 
you can do 2 health levels of damage if you connect the blow.
 
{WHack and Slash / Out of Character{x
{WSyntax:  {c[Automatic]{x
Your Potence rating is automatically added to your damage rolls for auto-
attacks, as well as some other Strength damage based attacks.

See also:  Brujah, Lasombra, Nosferatu
~
1 PRESENCE~

PRESENCE - THE POWER TO CONTROL EMOTION
 
A vampire with the Presence Discipline is exceptionally attractive and 
appealing to others. People want to be around the vampire, to bask in the 
brilliant light he sheds. He need not make any sort of overt or deliberate 
action, for Presence is a natural aspect of one's personality. Presence is a 
powerful, if subtle, Discipline.
 
The Presence Discipline is a power over the emotions of people, not their 
judgment or reason. Orders may not be given using Presence; the effect is 
completely nonverbal. Presence causes others to feel things or react in certain 
ways toward the vampire, but direct manipulation of the mind is the domain of 
Dominate.
 
Unlike Dominate, it can be used on many people at the same time, nor is eye 
contact required for it to be effective. The vampire needs to be clearly in 
sight of those he wishes to affect, however, as his face must be seen clearly.
 
Those affected by Presence can use Willpower points to resist the effects for a 
turn, as with Dominate. During this time they are able to turn around, thereby 
escaping the effects more permanently. Kindred are usually savvy enough to do 
so, but mortals seldom are.
 
